' tkHost -- the widget core every tkControls control runs on: SDL windows ("surfaces"), a
' widget TREE in each, and the services Win32 used to provide for free -- hit testing, hot
' tracking, capture, focus and Tab order, timers, invalidation, per-monitor scale, popups,
' modal dialogs, text input, cursors and the clipboard.
'
' THE MESSAGE MODEL IS WIN32'S ON PURPOSE. A widget is a state pointer plus a WidgetProc that
' receives TKM_* messages shaped like the WM_* ones it replaced, so a PsControls WndProc ports
' case for case. What changes is who sends them: this file, from SDL events. The logic of the
' tree, dispatch and popup rules follows PsPlatform's ui/core (PsWidget, PsDispatch,
' PsPaintWalk, PsPopupHost, PsModalHost), restated in this message model.
'
' COORDINATES
'   * A widget's x/y are relative to its PARENT (the surface root for a top-level widget, whose
'     origin is the window's), in device pixels. tkWidget_AbsRect gives window pixels.
'   * SDL reports mouse positions in WINDOW COORDINATES -- pixels on Windows, points on
'     Wayland/macOS -- so every event is multiplied by SDL_GetWindowPixelDensity first.
'   * Messages carry widget-LOCAL pixel coordinates, as Win32 client coordinates did.
'
' SURFACES. Every OS window is a TK_HOST: the main window, each popup (menus, dropdowns,
' tooltips) and each modal dialog. Each has its own renderer, text engine, widget tree, focus,
' capture and hot widget. One global router hands each SDL event to the surface whose window
' it names, so a host never sees another window's events by mistake.
'
' VIRTUAL SURFACES (docs/tiko-android A5, D-A5-1). Android's SDL has ONE window: a popup window
' cannot be made (SDL_CreatePopupWindow fails, so a combo box opened and closed at once) and nor
' can a dialog or a second form. With virtual surfaces on -- always on Android, TK_VIRTUAL=1
' elsewhere, which is how the self-tests exercise them on the desktop -- every surface after the
' first main window is a rectangle INSIDE it (bVirtual, pBase, vx/vy/vw/vh in the base's
' pixels): it shares the base's renderer and text engine, is painted after the base's own tree in
' creation order (so a submenu is above its menu), and is handed the events that land in it --
' the router translates them into its own pixels, so widgets and controls cannot tell. Each also
' has a window id of its own that no SDL window has (from &h40000000): an event that NAMES it -- a
' test's, or code addressing that surface -- goes to it directly, in its own coordinates, exactly as
' one addressed to a hidden window still reaches it on the desktop; only events naming the real
' window are routed by position. A second
' tkHost_Create is a PAGE: a virtual main surface covering the whole window, on top of the one
' before (D-A5-2). Everything that is a window operation on the desktop (show, hide, modal,
' raise, drag) is a flag here.
'
' THE SAFE AREA. With virtual surfaces on, a window's own tree lives in its safe area (ix, iy and
' root->cw/ch, from SDL_GetWindowSafeArea): Android 15's windows run under the status and
' navigation bars, and the first row of every demo was under the clock. The tree is painted
' through a viewport there, tkHost_PixelSize answers its size, and pointer events are moved into
' it, exactly as for a virtual surface. On the desktop the safe area is the whole window: 0, 0.
'
' TOUCH (D-A5-3). SDL turns a finger into the mouse, so a tap is a click everywhere already. The
' gesture layer adds what a phone expects, and touches no control. SDL sends its touch-mouse
' events before the finger's own; the layer HOLDS the press, as Android's tap timeout does:
'   a finger that lifts first is a tap -- press and release, a click
'   one still down after TK_PRESS_DELAY_MS gets its press (a scroll thumb, a splitter, a text
'     selection drag as on the desktop)
'   one that moves past the slop first is a SCROLL: no press at all -- a list selected the row a
'     swipe began on when the press went through at once (measured) -- and the movement becomes
'     fractional TKM_MOUSEWHEEL at the first point, so whatever scrolls under the finger, or an
'     ancestor that does, scrolls, with a fling after the finger lifts; a press already delivered
'     is cancelled with a release far outside (a button sees a press slid off)
'   one held still for TK_LONGPRESS_MS is the right button there: a context menu opens
' Touch-mouse motion is held back until a press is delivered, so a touch makes no hover, and a
' finger that lifts is the pointer leaving the window: a hover tooltip opened under a finger
' that had gone (measured).
'
' BACK (Android's button, SDLK_AC_BACK, trapped from SDL) goes back one level: the top popup
' closes, else the top dialog or page is asked to close as its close button would, else the
' window is.
#module "tkHost"

#import "../tkPaint" public
using tkPaint

' ==========================================================================================
' The bundled fonts
' ==========================================================================================
' tkControls ships its own fonts, so a program looks the same on every OS: Inter for text
' (SIL OFL 1.1), Cascadia Mono for code (SIL OFL 1.1) and Fluent UI System Icons for glyphs
' (MIT). They live in pkg/vendor/tkControls/fonts, and tiko copies them beside every program
' that imports tkHost ('runtime' in pkg/vendor/tiko.toml), so tkHost_FontDir() & TK_FONT_UI
' is a file that is there.
public const TK_FONT_UI = "Inter-Regular.ttf"
public const TK_FONT_UI_BOLD = "Inter-Bold.ttf"
public const TK_FONT_UI_ITALIC = "Inter-Italic.ttf"
public const TK_FONT_MONO = "CascadiaMono-Regular.ttf"
public const TK_FONT_ICONS = "FluentSystemIcons-Regular.ttf"

' Glyphs of TK_FONT_ICONS (its 20-pixel "regular" set), for wchr(): every glyph a control
' draws by default, and the common ones a host puts on buttons, toolbars and tabs.
public const TK_ICON_CHEVRON_DOWN = &hF2A3
public const TK_ICON_CHEVRON_RIGHT = &hF2B0
public const TK_ICON_MORE = &hE824                  ' the horizontal ellipsis
public const TK_ICON_CALENDAR = &hE24E
public const TK_ICON_INFO = &hF4A3
public const TK_ICON_WARNING = &hF869
public const TK_ICON_ERROR = &hF3F1
public const TK_ICON_QUESTION = &hF63D               ' in a circle
public const TK_ICON_CLOSE = &hF369
public const TK_ICON_CHECKBOX = &hF291
public const TK_ICON_CHECKBOX_CHECKED = &hF28D
public const TK_ICON_CHECKMARK = &hF294
public const TK_ICON_SAVE = &hF67F
public const TK_ICON_REFRESH = &hF13D
public const TK_ICON_SETTINGS = &hF6A9
public const TK_ICON_FOLDER = &hF418
public const TK_ICON_FOLDER_OPEN = &hF42E
public const TK_ICON_OPEN = &hF582
public const TK_ICON_DOCUMENT = &hF378
public const TK_ICON_PAGE = &hE557                   ' a document with lines
public const TK_ICON_PLAY = &hF605
public const TK_ICON_STOP = &hF72A
public const TK_ICON_DELETE = &hF34C
public const TK_ICON_STAR = &hF70F
public const TK_ICON_LOCK = &hE78F
public const TK_ICON_SEARCH = &hF68F
public const TK_ICON_BUG = &hE206
public const TK_ICON_CONSOLE = &hEE6F
public const TK_ICON_WRENCH = &hEE86
public const TK_ICON_WRAP = &hED69
public const TK_ICON_HELP = &hF638                   ' a bare question mark
public const TK_ICON_ALIGN_LEFT = &hF79F
public const TK_ICON_ALIGN_CENTER = &hF799
public const TK_ICON_ALIGN_RIGHT = &hF7A1
public const TK_ICON_BOLD = &hF7A4
public const TK_ICON_LIKE = &hF81F

' The command modifier as an SDL_Keymod mask: Cmd on macOS, Ctrl elsewhere. A control's command
' chords (copy, paste, undo, select all, word moves, add to a selection) test this, never
' SDL_KMOD_CTRL, so a Mac keyboard drives them with Cmd -- the rule tkCodeEdit (Scintilla's Ctrl)
' and tkKeys_Primary follow too.
#if defined( TIKO_OS_MACOS )
public const TK_KMOD_PRIMARY = SDL_KMOD_GUI
#else
public const TK_KMOD_PRIMARY = SDL_KMOD_CTRL
#endif

' Where the bundled fonts are: the program's own directory, with its separator.
public function tkHost_FontDir() as ustring
    dim as const zstring ptr base_ = SDL_GetBasePath()
    if base_ = 0 then return ""
    return *base_
end function

public enum
    TKM_PAINT = 1
    TKM_SIZE
    TKM_MOUSEMOVE
    TKM_MOUSEENTER
    TKM_MOUSELEAVE
    TKM_LBUTTONDOWN          ' m->clicks = 2 for a double click (SDL's count)
    TKM_LBUTTONUP
    TKM_RBUTTONDOWN
    TKM_RBUTTONUP
    TKM_MBUTTONDOWN
    TKM_MBUTTONUP
    TKM_MOUSEWHEEL           ' m->wheelX / wheelY in notches; BUBBLES to the parent if refused
    TKM_CAPTURECHANGED
    TKM_SETFOCUS             ' m->pOther = the widget losing focus
    TKM_KILLFOCUS            ' m->pOther = the widget gaining it
    TKM_KEYDOWN              ' m->key (SDL_Keycode), m->mods, m->bFlag = repeat; BUBBLES if refused
    TKM_KEYUP
    TKM_CHAR                 ' m->text = UTF-8 text from SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT
    TKM_IMECOMPOSE           ' m->text = the pre-edit string, m->nStart/nLen its cursor/selection
    TKM_ENABLE               ' m->bFlag = new state
    TKM_SHOW                 ' m->bFlag = new state
    TKM_TIMER                ' m->timerId
    TKM_SCALECHANGED         ' m->fOld / fNew
    TKM_THEMECHANGED
    TKM_DESTROY
    TKM_DROPFILES            ' files dropped from the OS: m->text = their paths, LF-separated (UTF-8),
                             ' m->nStart = how many, m->x / y = the drop point; BUBBLES if refused
    TKM_DROPTEXT             ' text dropped from the OS: m->text, m->x / y; BUBBLES if refused
    TKM_CONTEXTMENU          ' to a CONTEXT-MENU COMPONENT (tkWidget_SetContextMenu): m->pOther = the widget
                             ' it opens for, m->x / y = where, in the surface's window pixels; m->bFlag =
                             ' from the keyboard (the Menu key, Shift+F10)
    TKM_ADORNLAYOUT          ' to an ADORNMENT just before it paints: place yourself against your parent
                             ' (the target) as it is now. Invalidations made while handling it are
                             ' dropped: this frame already paints the new rect.
end enum

public enum
    TK_SURF_MAIN = 0
    TK_SURF_POPUP            ' menus, dropdowns: dismissed by Esc or a press elsewhere
    TK_SURF_TOOLTIP          ' never takes input, never dismissed by the router
    TK_SURF_DIALOG           ' modal, run by tkHost_RunModal
end enum

public enum
    TK_CURSOR_ARROW = 0
    TK_CURSOR_IBEAM
    TK_CURSOR_HAND
    TK_CURSOR_SIZEWE
    TK_CURSOR_SIZENS
    TK_CURSOR_SIZEALL
    TK_CURSOR_WAIT
    TK_CURSOR_SIZENWSE     ' a diagonal resize: top-left to bottom-right
    TK_CURSOR_SIZENESW     ' a diagonal resize: top-right to bottom-left
    TK_CURSOR_COUNT
end enum

' What a focused text widget's screen keyboard is (tkWidget_SetTextKind; docs/fasting-android F4).
public enum
    TK_TEXT_DEFAULT = 0      ' SDL's default: multi-line text with autocorrect (what every widget had)
    TK_TEXT_LINE             ' one line of text
    TK_TEXT_MULTILINE        ' paragraphs; sentences capitalised
    TK_TEXT_DECIMAL          ' a number with a point (and a sign)
    TK_TEXT_INTEGER          ' a whole number (and a sign)
    TK_TEXT_PASSWORD         ' hidden, never learned by the keyboard
end enum

' Reserved timer ids. A control's own ids start at TK_TIMER_APP.
public enum
    TK_TIMER_CARET = 900
    TK_TIMER_AUTOREPEAT
    TK_TIMER_AUTOSCROLL
    TK_TIMER_MARQUEE
    TK_TIMER_HOVER
    TK_TIMER_TIPSHOW
    TK_TIMER_TIPPOP
    TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART     ' the host's own: a field of another keyboard kind (F4)
    TK_TIMER_APP = 1000
end enum

public type TK_HOST as TK_HOST_
public type TK_WIDGET as TK_WIDGET_

' A widget's mouse-move watcher (tkWidget_SetMouseMoveCallback): x, y in pixels from w's top-left,
' buttons SDL's button mask, mods SDL's modifier keys.
public type TK_MouseMoveSub as sub( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval x as long, byval y as long, byval buttons as long, byval mods as long )

public type TK_MSG
    msg      as long
    x        as single          ' widget-local pixels (mouse messages)
    y        as single
    clicks   as long            ' button messages: 1, 2 for a double click
    wheelX   as single          ' TKM_MOUSEWHEEL, notches (fractional on precise devices)
    wheelY   as single
    key      as long            ' SDL_Keycode (TKM_KEYDOWN / KEYUP)
    mods     as long            ' SDL_Keymod
    timerId  as long            ' TKM_TIMER
    bFlag    as boolean         ' TKM_ENABLE / TKM_SHOW: the new state; TKM_KEYDOWN: repeat
    fOld     as single          ' TKM_SCALECHANGED
    fNew     as single
    text     as string          ' TKM_CHAR / TKM_IMECOMPOSE: UTF-8
    nStart   as long            ' TKM_IMECOMPOSE
    nLen     as long
    pOther   as TK_WIDGET ptr   ' TKM_SETFOCUS / KILLFOCUS: the other party
    pPaint   as TK_PAINT ptr    ' TKM_PAINT
    scancode as long            ' TKM_KEYDOWN / KEYUP: SDL_Scancode -- the physical key, for chords
                                ' matched on the unshifted key (tkKeys)
end type

public type tkWidgetProc as function( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval m as TK_MSG ptr ) as boolean
public type tkHostPaintSub as sub( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval p as TK_PAINT ptr )
public type tkHostSub as sub( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
public type tkHostCloseFunc as function( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
' A key down BEFORE the focused widget sees it: TRUE = handled (Win32's TranslateAccelerator slot).
public type tkHostKeyFunc as function( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval m as TK_MSG ptr ) as boolean
' Files or text dropped where no widget claimed them: TKM_DROPFILES / TKM_DROPTEXT, window pixels.
public type tkHostDropSub as sub( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval m as TK_MSG ptr )
' Told after the surface's size or scale changed (tkHost_AddSizeHook): pUser is what was added.
public type tkHostSizeHookSub as sub( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval pUser as any ptr )

public type TK_WIDGET_
    pHost         as TK_HOST ptr
    pParent       as TK_WIDGET ptr      ' 0 only for a surface's root
    pFirst        as TK_WIDGET ptr      ' children, in z-order: the LAST is on top
    pLast         as TK_WIDGET ptr
    pNext         as TK_WIDGET ptr
    pPrev         as TK_WIDGET ptr
    x             as long               ' parent-relative pixels
    y             as long
    cw            as long
    ch            as long
    ctrlId        as long
    isEnabled     as boolean = true
    isVisible     as boolean = true
    isFocusable   as boolean = false
    nTabIndex     as long = 0           ' its place among its siblings in Tab order; 0 = none (tree order, after)
    bClipChildren as boolean = true
    bWantsText    as boolean = false    ' focus here starts SDL text input (and the IME)
    nTextKind     as long = 0           ' TK_TEXT_*: the screen keyboard a focused text widget asks for
    cursor        as long = TK_CURSOR_ARROW
    proc          as tkWidgetProc
    pData         as any ptr            ' the control's own state
    ' tkTheme's, opaque here: one plain (callocate'd) block each, freed by tkWidget_Destroy.
    pThemeScope   as any ptr            ' a theme for this subtree (tkTheme_ApplyTo); 0 = inherit
    pColorRecipe  as any ptr            ' per-field colour overrides (tkTheme_SetRecipe)
    pContextMenu  as TK_WIDGET ptr      ' the component that is this widget's right-click menu, 0 = none
    pOnMouseMove  as TK_MouseMoveSub    ' told of moves over it, and over descendants with none of their own
    bAdorner      as boolean = false    ' an ADORNMENT of its parent (tkWidget_SetAdorner): painted after the
                                        ' parent's subtree with the parent's own clip, never hit-tested
end type

public type TK_FONT
    f   as TTF_Font ptr
    pt  as single
end type

public type TK_TIMER
    pW     as TK_WIDGET ptr
    id     as long
    sdlId  as SDL_TimerID
    gen    as long              ' bumped on kill, so a queued tick for a dead timer is dropped
    active as boolean
end type

public type TK_HOST_
    kind         as long = TK_SURF_MAIN
    pOwner       as TK_HOST ptr       ' popups and dialogs: the surface they belong to
    bVirtual     as boolean           ' a rectangle inside pBase's window, not a window (see top)
    pBase        as TK_HOST ptr       ' virtual: the real surface whose window and renderer it uses
    vx           as long              ' virtual: its rectangle, in pBase's pixels
    vy           as long
    vw           as long
    vh           as long
    bShown       as boolean           ' virtual: tkHost_Show'n and not hidden
    sTitle       as string            ' virtual: the title a window would have shown (UTF-8)
    ix           as long              ' a window with virtual surfaces: its safe area's corner,
    iy           as long              ' in window pixels (see top); its size is root->cw/ch
    win          as SDL_Window ptr
    renderer     as SDL_Renderer ptr
    engine       as TTF_TextEngine ptr
    winId        as SDL_WindowID
    root         as TK_WIDGET ptr     ' covers the window; top-level widgets are its children
    fScale       as single = 1        ' design units -> pixels
    fDensity     as single = 1        ' SDL event coordinates -> pixels
    fScaleForced as single = 0        ' > 0 pins fScale (the self-tests' 1.75 pass)
    pHot         as TK_WIDGET ptr
    pFocus       as TK_WIDGET ptr
    pCapture     as TK_WIDGET ptr
    pLastDown    as TK_WIDGET ptr     ' for demoting a double click that changed widgets
    bCaptureOS   as boolean           ' did SDL_CaptureMouse succeed for the live capture?
    bTextInput   as boolean
    nTextKindOn  as long              ' the TK_TEXT_* the live text input was started with
    bDirty       as boolean = true
    bQuit        as boolean
    bClosed      as boolean           ' closed, waiting to be reaped after this event
    bEndModal    as boolean
    bPassDismissClick as boolean      ' popups: the press that dismisses this one still reaches
                                      ' its target (vendor PsPopupMenu); default: consumed
    bKeepOnFocusLoss as boolean       ' popups: NOT closed when focus leaves the application -- a
                                      ' modal popup (tkColorPicker) ends only on a press outside
    nModalResult as long
    lastX        as single            ' last mouse position, window pixels
    lastY        as single
    buttonsDown  as long              ' bit 0 left, 1 right, 2 middle: held now
    clrBack      as ulong = &hFF21252Bul
    pDefaultFont as TTF_Font ptr      ' the DEFAULT_GUI_FONT analogue
    fonts(any)   as TK_FONT
    rcDrag       as TKRECT            ' window pixels; a press here drags the window (dialogs)
    nFrames      as long              ' frames rendered, for the idle-CPU claim
    bResumed     as boolean           ' back in the foreground: the next render presents twice
    pUser        as any ptr           ' the host's own payload
    OnPaint      as tkHostPaintSub    ' the surface's own background (labels, hairlines)
    OnSize       as tkHostSub
    OnScale      as tkHostSub
    OnClosed     as tkHostSub         ' popups: fired once when it closes, for any reason
    OnCloseRequest as tkHostCloseFunc ' the OS close button (dialogs and main windows); TRUE = handled, stays open
    OnPreKey     as tkHostKeyFunc     ' accelerators: asked before the focused widget (tkKeys_Attach)
    OnDrop       as tkHostDropSub     ' a drop no widget claimed (the surface's own: open the files)
    sDropFiles   as string            ' a drop in progress: the paths so far, LF-separated
    nDropFiles   as long
    sDropText    as string
    ' MORE SIZE WATCHERS than OnSize's one slot (which tkApp's form owns): a toaster keeping its
    ' cards in a corner. Run after OnSize on every path that runs it, live resize included.
    sizeHooks(0 to 3)    as tkHostSizeHookSub
    sizeHookData(0 to 3) as any ptr
end type


' ---- module state: every live surface, the timer pool, cursors ---------------------------
dim shared as TK_HOST ptr gHosts(0 to 63)
dim shared as long gnHosts
dim shared as TK_TIMER gTimers(0 to 255)
dim shared as Uint32 gEvTimer
dim shared as Uint32 gEvFocusCheck
dim shared as SDL_Cursor ptr gCursors(0 to TK_CURSOR_COUNT - 1)
dim shared as long gCursorNow = -1
dim shared as long gTrace = -1
dim shared as ulong gPressSerial          ' +1 per mouse press, BEFORE the dismissal rule runs
dim shared as long gDispatching           ' >0: an event is being delivered, so a surface is on the stack
dim shared as long gVirtual = -1          ' virtual surfaces: -1 not yet decided, 0 off, 1 on (see top)
dim shared as TK_HOST ptr gMouseHost      ' the surface the last pointer event went to (virtual)
dim shared as SDL_WindowID gVirtualIdNext = &h40000000ul   ' virtual surfaces' own window ids

' Are surfaces virtual? Decided once: always on Android, which has one window; elsewhere only
' when TK_VIRTUAL=1 asks, so the desktop's own behaviour is exactly what it was.
private function Virtual_() as boolean
    if gVirtual < 0 then
        #ifdef TIKO_OS_ANDROID
            gVirtual = 1
        #else
            gVirtual = iif( environ( "TK_VIRTUAL" ) = "1", 1, 0 )
        #endif
    end if
    return gVirtual = 1
end function

' Are surfaces virtual in this process (Android; TK_VIRTUAL=1)?
public function tkHost_VirtualSurfaces() as boolean
    return Virtual_()
end function

public function tkHost_IsVirtual( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    return (h <> 0) andalso h->bVirtual
end function

' Called with each renderer just before it is destroyed, so caches of textures that belong to
' it (tkImage) can drop them. One hook: the only client is tkImage.
public type tkRendererGoneSub as sub( byval r as SDL_Renderer ptr )
dim shared as tkRendererGoneSub gOnRendererGone

' Adds a size watcher to h: f( h, pUser ) runs after h's size or scale changed, after OnSize --
' including inside Windows' live-resize loop. Up to 4 per surface; adding the same pair twice is
' one. FALSE when all 4 are taken.
public function tkHost_AddSizeHook( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval f as tkHostSizeHookSub, byval pUser as any ptr = 0 ) as boolean
    if (h = 0) orelse (f = 0) then return false
    for i as long = 0 to 3
        if (h->sizeHooks(i) = f) andalso (h->sizeHookData(i) = pUser) then return true
    next
    for i as long = 0 to 3
        if h->sizeHooks(i) = 0 then
            h->sizeHooks(i) = f
            h->sizeHookData(i) = pUser
            return true
        end if
    next
    return false
end function

public sub tkHost_RemoveSizeHook( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval f as tkHostSizeHookSub, byval pUser as any ptr = 0 )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    for i as long = 0 to 3
        if (h->sizeHooks(i) = f) andalso (h->sizeHookData(i) = pUser) then
            h->sizeHooks(i) = 0
            h->sizeHookData(i) = 0
        end if
    next
end sub

private sub RunSizeHooks_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    for i as long = 0 to 3
        if h->sizeHooks(i) then h->sizeHooks(i)( h, h->sizeHookData(i) )
    next
end sub

public sub tkHost_SetRendererGoneHook( byval f as tkRendererGoneSub )
    gOnRendererGone = f
end sub

' Called whenever a surface's hot widget changes (the widget under the mouse), so a watcher
' that does not subclass the widget -- tkTooltip -- can wake its clock. One hook.
public type tkHotChangedSub as sub( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
dim shared as tkHotChangedSub gOnHotChanged

public sub tkHost_SetHotChangedHook( byval f as tkHotChangedSub )
    gOnHotChanged = f
end sub

' Called after tkWidget_Show changed a widget's visibility (not when it was already in that
' state), so a watcher that does not subclass the widget -- tkLayout, whose hidden docks take no
' slice -- can place its siblings again. One hook.
public type tkShowChangedSub as sub( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval bShow as boolean )
dim shared as tkShowChangedSub gOnShowChanged

public sub tkHost_SetShowChangedHook( byval f as tkShowChangedSub )
    gOnShowChanged = f
end sub

' Offered every event tkHost_Dispatch sees, before anything else -- in tkHost_Run, in
' tkHost_Pump AND inside tkHost_RunModal's loop -- so an application layer (tkApp) can run its
' own user events and watch system events wherever the pump happens to be. TRUE consumes the
' event. One hook: the only client is tkApp.
public type tkEventHookFunc as function( byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean
dim shared as tkEventHookFunc gOnEvent

public sub tkHost_SetEventHook( byval f as tkEventHookFunc )
    gOnEvent = f
end sub

' MORE HOOKS, for modules below the application layer that deliver their own user events where
' the pump is (tkFileDialog: an answer from SDL's dialog thread). Asked after tkApp's, in the
' order added; TRUE consumes the event. Adding one twice is one.
dim shared as tkEventHookFunc gHooks( 0 to 7 )

public sub tkHost_AddEventHook( byval f as tkEventHookFunc )
    if f = 0 then exit sub
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gHooks )
        if gHooks(i) = f then exit sub
    next
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gHooks )
        if gHooks(i) = 0 then gHooks(i) = f : exit sub
    next
end sub

public sub tkHost_RemoveEventHook( byval f as tkEventHookFunc )
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gHooks )
        if gHooks(i) = f then gHooks(i) = 0
    next
end sub

declare function LiveResizeWatch( byval userdata as any ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean

private sub Register( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if gnHosts <= ubound( gHosts ) then gHosts(gnHosts) = h : gnHosts += 1
    static as boolean watching = false
    if watching = false then watching = SDL_AddEventWatch( @LiveResizeWatch, 0 )
end sub

private sub Unregister( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if gHosts(i) = h then
            for j as long = i to gnHosts - 2
                gHosts(j) = gHosts(j + 1)
            next
            gnHosts -= 1
            exit sub
        end if
    next
end sub

private function HostOfWindow( byval id as SDL_WindowID ) as TK_HOST ptr
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if (gHosts(i)->winId = id) andalso (gHosts(i)->bClosed = false) then return gHosts(i)
    next
    return 0
end function

' The serial of the press being dispatched (or the last one). A popup's OnClosed that reads it
' and a press handler that reads it again can tell "this press closed my popup" -- the guard
' that stops a click on the button that opened a popup from reopening it at once.
public function tkHost_PressSerial() as ulong
    return gPressSerial
end function

public function tkHost_Count() as long
    return gnHosts
end function


' ---- scale -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
public function tkHost_Scale( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval v as long ) as long
    if h = 0 then return v
    return cint( v * h->fScale )
end function

private sub UpdateScale( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    h->fDensity = SDL_GetWindowPixelDensity( h->win )
    if h->fDensity <= 0 then h->fDensity = 1
    if h->fScaleForced > 0 then
        h->fScale = h->fScaleForced
    elseif (h->pOwner <> 0) andalso (h->kind <> TK_SURF_DIALOG) then
        h->fScale = h->pOwner->fScale       ' a popup is drawn at its owner's scale
    else
        h->fScale = SDL_GetWindowDisplayScale( h->win )
        if h->fScale <= 0 then h->fScale = 1
    end if
end sub

' Fonts are sized in POINTS AT 96 DPI times the scale, which is what Win32's CreateFont(...,
' 10, ...) through AfxNova's DPI-aware helper produced -- so a 10pt caption is the same pixel
' height as the Win32 control's.
private sub SizeFont( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval f as TTF_Font ptr, byval pt as single )
    dim as long dpi = cint( 96 * h->fScale )
    TTF_SetFontSizeDPI( f, pt, dpi, dpi )
end sub

' RESOURCES: fonts and images known by a name. A program that carries them inside itself ('#embed')
' registers each one's bytes; one that ships them beside itself registers each one's file. Every font
' tkHost, tkApp and tkCodeEdit open, and every image tkImage, tkButton and tkForm_SetIcon load
' (tkHost_LoadSurface), takes a registered name where it takes a file path -- exactly that name,
' nothing derived from it. The conventions: "mem:<file name>" for a theme's fonts (tkApp's
' FontDir = "mem:" finds them by their usual file names), "res:<Name>" for a project's resources
' (the Form Designer's Resource Center). Bytes stay the caller's: they must outlive every font
' opened from them (an '#embed' array lives as long as the program).
dim shared as string gResName()
dim shared as const any ptr gResData()
dim shared as integer gResSize()
dim shared as string gResFile()

private function ResIndex_( byref name_ as string ) as long
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gResName )
        if gResName(i) = name_ then return i
    next
    return -1
end function

private function ResSlot_( byref name_ as string ) as long
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( name_ )
    if k >= 0 then return k
    k = ubound( gResName ) + 1
    redim preserve gResName( 0 to k ) : redim preserve gResData( 0 to k )
    redim preserve gResSize( 0 to k ) : redim preserve gResFile( 0 to k )
    gResName(k) = name_
    return k
end function

' 'name_' stands for these bytes (registered again, it is replaced).
public sub tkHost_AddResourceData( byref name_ as string, byval pData as const any ptr, byval nBytes as integer )
    dim as long k = ResSlot_( name_ )
    gResData(k) = pData : gResSize(k) = nBytes : gResFile(k) = ""
end sub

' 'name_' stands for this file (registered again, it is replaced).
public sub tkHost_AddResourceFile( byref name_ as string, byref file as ustring )
    dim as long k = ResSlot_( name_ )
    gResData(k) = 0 : gResSize(k) = 0 : gResFile(k) = file
end sub

' 'name_' no longer stands for anything. A font already opened from it stays as it is.
public sub tkHost_RemoveResource( byref name_ as string )
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( name_ ), n = ubound( gResName )
    if k < 0 then exit sub
    if k < n then
        gResName(k) = gResName(n) : gResData(k) = gResData(n)
        gResSize(k) = gResSize(n) : gResFile(k) = gResFile(n)
    end if
    if n = 0 then
        erase gResName, gResData, gResSize, gResFile
    else
        redim preserve gResName( 0 to n - 1 ) : redim preserve gResData( 0 to n - 1 )
        redim preserve gResSize( 0 to n - 1 ) : redim preserve gResFile( 0 to n - 1 )
    end if
end sub

' TRUE when 'name_' stands for something there: bytes, or a file that exists.
public function tkHost_HasResource( byref name_ as string ) as boolean
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( name_ )
    if k < 0 then return false
    if gResData(k) then return true
    if len( gResFile(k) ) = 0 then return false
    return SDL_GetPathInfo( strptr( gResFile(k) ), 0 )
end function

' The file a registered name stands for ("" for bytes, or a name not registered).
public function tkHost_ResourceFile( byref name_ as string ) as string
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( name_ )
    if k < 0 then return ""
    return gResFile(k)
end function

' A font's bytes under a name (tkHost_AddResourceData, by its older name).
public sub tkHost_AddFontData( byref name_ as string, byval pData as const any ptr, byval nBytes as integer )
    tkHost_AddResourceData( name_, pData, nBytes )
end sub

' TRUE when 'name_' was registered and is there: a font open takes it as a font that is there.
public function tkHost_HasFontData( byref name_ as string ) as boolean
    return tkHost_HasResource( name_ )
end function

' An image as a surface, from a registered name's bytes or file, or else from 'path' as a file:
' every format SDL_image reads. 0 when there is nothing to read, or it is not an image.
public function tkHost_LoadSurface( byref path as ustring ) as SDL_Surface ptr
    if len( path ) = 0 then return 0
    dim as string p8 = path
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( p8 )
    if k >= 0 then
        if gResData(k) then return IMG_Load_IO( SDL_IOFromConstMem( gResData(k), gResSize(k) ), true )
        p8 = gResFile(k)
        if len( p8 ) = 0 then return 0
    end if
    return IMG_Load( strptr( p8 ) )
end function

' A font file or a registered name, at 'pt' points (unscaled) and face 'face' of a collection.
' The one place a font is opened from a name, so a registered one is honoured everywhere.
' The font-source registry (tkHost_FontSource). A font's slot is reused when SDL_ttf hands out the
' same pointer again, so a font closed without tkHost_CloseFont leaves nothing that can mislead.
dim shared as TTF_Font ptr gFontSrcF()
dim shared as string gFontSrcPath()
dim shared as long gFontSrcFace()
dim shared as long gnFontSrc

private sub NoteFontSource_( byval f as TTF_Font ptr, byref path as string, byval face as long )
    dim as long k = -1
    for i as long = 0 to gnFontSrc - 1
        if gFontSrcF(i) = f then k = i : exit for
    next
    if k < 0 then
        k = gnFontSrc
        if k > ubound( gFontSrcF ) then
            dim as long n = iif( k < 16, 16, k * 2 )
            redim preserve gFontSrcF( 0 to n - 1 )
            redim preserve gFontSrcPath( 0 to n - 1 )
            redim preserve gFontSrcFace( 0 to n - 1 )
        end if
        gnFontSrc += 1
    end if
    gFontSrcF(k) = f : gFontSrcPath(k) = path : gFontSrcFace(k) = face
end sub

private sub ForgetFontSource_( byval f as TTF_Font ptr )
    for i as long = 0 to gnFontSrc - 1
        if gFontSrcF(i) = f then
            gnFontSrc -= 1
            gFontSrcF(i) = gFontSrcF(gnFontSrc) : gFontSrcPath(i) = gFontSrcPath(gnFontSrc)
            gFontSrcFace(i) = gFontSrcFace(gnFontSrc)
            gFontSrcPath(gnFontSrc) = ""
            exit sub
        end if
    next
end sub

public function tkHost_OpenFontFace( byref path as string, byval pt as single, byval face as long ) as TTF_Font ptr
    dim as SDL_PropertiesID props = SDL_CreateProperties()
    if props = 0 then return 0
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( path )
    if (k >= 0) andalso (gResData(k) <> 0) then
        SDL_SetPointerProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_IOSTREAM_POINTER, SDL_IOFromConstMem( gResData(k), gResSize(k) ) )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_IOSTREAM_AUTOCLOSE_BOOLEAN, true )
    elseif k >= 0 then
        SDL_SetStringProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_FILENAME_STRING, strptr( gResFile(k) ) )
    else
        SDL_SetStringProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_FILENAME_STRING, strptr( path ) )
    end if
    SDL_SetFloatProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_SIZE_FLOAT, pt )
    SDL_SetNumberProperty( props, TTF_PROP_FONT_CREATE_FACE_NUMBER, face )
    dim as TTF_Font ptr f = TTF_OpenFontWithProperties( props )
    SDL_DestroyProperties( props )
    if f then NoteFontSource_( f, path, face )
    return f
end function

' Where a font came from: the name or path tkHost_OpenFontFace was given, and the face. tkPrint
' re-opens a recorded font at a page's size this way (and a PDF writer will embed its bytes).
' FALSE for a font SDL_ttf opened without tkHost.
public function tkHost_FontSource( byval f as TTF_Font ptr, byref path as string, byref face as long ) as boolean
    if f = 0 then return false
    for i as long = 0 to gnFontSrc - 1
        if gFontSrcF(i) = f then path = gFontSrcPath(i) : face = gFontSrcFace(i) : return true
    next
    return false
end function

' A font file's bytes, by the name or path tkHost_OpenFontFace takes: a registered resource's own
' bytes (bOwned = FALSE: they live as long as the registration), else the file read whole
' (bOwned = TRUE: SDL_free them). FALSE when there is nothing to read. For a PDF writer's embedding.
public function tkHost_FontBytes( byref path as string, byref pData as const any ptr, byref nBytes as integer, _
                                  byref bOwned as boolean ) as boolean
    pData = 0 : nBytes = 0 : bOwned = false
    dim as string file = path
    dim as long k = ResIndex_( path )
    if k >= 0 then
        if gResData(k) then
            pData = gResData(k) : nBytes = gResSize(k)
            return nBytes > 0
        end if
        file = gResFile(k)
    end if
    if len( file ) = 0 then return false
    dim as uinteger sz
    dim as any ptr p = SDL_LoadFile( strptr( file ), @sz )
    if p = 0 then return false
    pData = p : nBytes = sz : bOwned = true
    return true
end function

' Close a font tkHost_OpenFontFace opened, and forget where it came from.
public sub tkHost_CloseFont( byval f as TTF_Font ptr )
    if f = 0 then exit sub
    ForgetFontSource_( f )
    TTF_CloseFont( f )
end sub

public function tkHost_OpenFont( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byref path as ustring, byval pt as single ) as TTF_Font ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    dim as string p8 = path
    dim as TTF_Font ptr f = tkHost_OpenFontFace( p8, pt, 0 )
    if f = 0 then return 0
    SizeFont( h, f, pt )
    dim as long n = ubound( h->fonts ) + 1
    redim preserve h->fonts( 0 to n )
    h->fonts(n).f = f
    h->fonts(n).pt = pt
    return f
end function


' ---- creation ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
private function NewRoot( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr r = new TK_WIDGET
    r->pHost = h
    return r
end function

private sub SizeRoot( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as long pw, ph
    if h->bVirtual then
        pw = h->vw : ph = h->vh
    else
        SDL_GetRenderOutputSize( h->renderer, @pw, @ph )
        h->ix = 0 : h->iy = 0
        if Virtual_() then
            dim as SDL_Rect sa
            if SDL_GetWindowSafeArea( h->win, @sa ) andalso (sa.w > 0) andalso (sa.h > 0) then
                h->ix = cint( sa.x * h->fDensity ) : h->iy = cint( sa.y * h->fDensity )
                pw = cint( sa.w * h->fDensity ) : ph = cint( sa.h * h->fDensity )
            end if
            ' TK_SAFE_INSET=l,t,r,b (pixels): a safe area on a desktop, whose is the whole window --
            ' how the inset is tested off Android
            dim as string si = environ( "TK_SAFE_INSET" )
            if len( si ) then
                dim as long l, t, r, b, k1 = instr( si, "," ), k2 = instr( k1 + 1, si, "," ), k3 = instr( k2 + 1, si, "," )
                if (k1 > 0) andalso (k2 > 0) andalso (k3 > 0) then
                    l = valint( left( si, k1 - 1 ) ) : t = valint( mid( si, k1 + 1, k2 - k1 - 1 ) )
                    r = valint( mid( si, k2 + 1, k3 - k2 - 1 ) ) : b = valint( mid( si, k3 + 1 ) )
                    h->ix = l : h->iy = t : pw -= l + r : ph -= t + b
                end if
            end if
        end if
    end if
    h->root->cw = pw : h->root->ch = ph
end sub

' The real surface a new virtual one draws in: the owner's base, or the owner itself; with no
' owner (a page, an ownerless dialog), the first real main window.
private function BaseOf_( byval owner as TK_HOST ptr ) as TK_HOST ptr
    if owner then return iif( owner->bVirtual, owner->pBase, owner )
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if (gHosts(i)->bVirtual = false) andalso (gHosts(i)->bClosed = false) then return gHosts(i)
    next
    return 0
end function

' A virtual surface: base's window, renderer and text engine; rectangle x, y, w, hgt in BASE
' pixels. Hidden until tkHost_Show, like a window.
private function FinishVirtual_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval base_ as TK_HOST ptr, _
                                 byval x as long, byval y as long, byval w as long, byval hgt as long ) as boolean
    if base_ = 0 then return false
    h->bVirtual = true
    h->pBase = base_
    h->win = base_->win
    h->winId = gVirtualIdNext             ' named only by events addressed to it (see top)
    gVirtualIdNext += 1
    h->renderer = base_->renderer
    h->engine = base_->engine
    h->vx = x : h->vy = y : h->vw = w : h->vh = hgt
    h->fDensity = base_->fDensity
    if h->fScaleForced > 0 then
        h->fScale = h->fScaleForced
    else
        h->fScale = iif( h->pOwner <> 0, h->pOwner->fScale, base_->fScale )
    end if
    h->root = NewRoot( h )
    SizeRoot( h )
    if gEvTimer = 0 then gEvTimer = SDL_RegisterEvents( 1 )
    Register( h )
    return true
end function

private function FinishSurface( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    h->winId = SDL_GetWindowID( h->win )
    h->renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer( h->win, 0 )
    if h->renderer = 0 then return false
    SDL_SetRenderDrawBlendMode( h->renderer, SDL_BLENDMODE_BLEND )
    h->engine = TTF_CreateRendererTextEngine( h->renderer )
    h->root = NewRoot( h )
    SizeRoot( h )
    if gEvTimer = 0 then gEvTimer = SDL_RegisterEvents( 1 )
    Register( h )
    return true
end function

' The main window. w, h in DESIGN units, like CWindow.Create's: it comes out w*scale by h*scale
' pixels.
public function tkHost_Create( byref title as ustring, byval w as long, byval hgt as long, _
                               byref defaultFont as ustring, byval forcedScale as single = 0 ) as TK_HOST ptr
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = new TK_HOST
    h->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN
    h->fScaleForced = forcedScale
    ' A SECOND MAIN WINDOW WITH VIRTUAL SURFACES IS A PAGE over the whole window (D-A5-2).
    if Virtual_() then
        dim as TK_HOST ptr b = BaseOf_( 0 )
        if b then
            h->clrBack = b->clrBack
            h->sTitle = title
            if FinishVirtual_( h, b, 0, 0, b->root->cw, b->root->ch ) = false then delete h : return 0
            if len( defaultFont ) then h->pDefaultFont = tkHost_OpenFont( h, defaultFont, 9 )
            return h
        end if
    end if
    ' The close button is OnCloseRequest's alone (DispatchTo: not vetoed = bQuit). By default SDL
    ' also queues a QUIT behind its last window's close request; a modal box opened from the veto
    ' ("save the changes?") then takes that QUIT in tkHost_RunModal, ends as 0 and re-posts it, and
    ' the app quits past the veto (tkEdit, 2026-10-27). SDL reads the hint when a close is requested.
    SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_QUIT_ON_LAST_WINDOW_CLOSE, "0" )
    ' ANDROID'S BACK BUTTON comes to tkHost as SDLK_AC_BACK (Back_) instead of ending the Activity.
    #ifdef TIKO_OS_ANDROID
        SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON, "1" )
    #endif
    dim as string t8 = title
    ' ANDROID'S ONE WINDOW IS THE ACTIVITY, on screen whatever SDL is told; created HIDDEN, SDL skips
    ' every draw until tkHost_Show, so a back buffer read before it held zeros (measured, A5 step 7)
    ' where a hidden desktop window renders all the same.
    #ifdef TIKO_OS_ANDROID
        dim as SDL_WindowFlags hid = 0
    #else
        dim as SDL_WindowFlags hid = SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN
    #endif
    h->win = SDL_CreateWindow( strptr( t8 ), w, hgt, SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY or SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE or hid )
    if h->win = 0 then delete h : return 0
    UpdateScale( h )
    ' Resize to the design size now the scale is known. The size is in WINDOW coordinates, so
    ' divide the pixel target by the density.
    SDL_SetWindowSize( h->win, cint( w * h->fScale / h->fDensity ), cint( hgt * h->fScale / h->fDensity ) )
    if FinishSurface( h ) = false then SDL_DestroyWindow( h->win ) : delete h : return 0
    if len( defaultFont ) then h->pDefaultFont = tkHost_OpenFont( h, defaultFont, 9 )
    return h
end function

' Is h's window always on top? A window that belongs to one has to be too, or it opens BEHIND it
' (Windows: a menu's drop-down under an always-on-top form, a message box under its owner).
private function OnTop_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    return (h <> 0) andalso (h->win <> 0) andalso ((SDL_GetWindowFlags( h->win ) and SDL_WINDOW_ALWAYS_ON_TOP) <> 0)
end function

' A popup (TK_SURF_POPUP) or tooltip (TK_SURF_TOOLTIP) window of `owner`. x, y, w, h are OWNER
' window pixels; see tkHost_PlacePopup to compute them against an anchor. It is created
' hidden and EMPTY: add widgets to it, then tkHost_Show. Wayland cannot re-show an unmapped
' popup, so a popup is created per open and closed (tkHost_Close) per dismissal.
public function tkHost_CreatePopup( byval owner as TK_HOST ptr, byval x as long, byval y as long, _
                                    byval w as long, byval hgt as long, byval kind as long = TK_SURF_POPUP, _
                                    byval extraFlags as Uint64 = 0 ) as TK_HOST ptr
    if (owner = 0) orelse (w <= 0) orelse (hgt <= 0) then return 0
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = new TK_HOST
    h->kind = kind
    h->pOwner = owner
    h->pDefaultFont = owner->pDefaultFont
    h->clrBack = owner->clrBack
    if Virtual_() then
        dim as long ox = 0, oy = 0
        if owner->bVirtual then ox = owner->vx : oy = owner->vy
        if FinishVirtual_( h, BaseOf_( owner ), ox + x, oy + y, w, hgt ) = false then delete h : return 0
        return h
    end if
    dim as Uint64 fl = SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY or SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN or extraFlags
    fl or= iif( kind = TK_SURF_TOOLTIP, SDL_WINDOW_TOOLTIP, SDL_WINDOW_POPUP_MENU )
    if OnTop_( owner ) then fl or= SDL_WINDOW_ALWAYS_ON_TOP
    dim as single d = owner->fDensity
    h->win = SDL_CreatePopupWindow( owner->win, cint( x / d ), cint( y / d ), cint( w / d ), cint( hgt / d ), fl )
    if h->win = 0 then
        if gTrace = 1 then print "SDL_CreatePopupWindow failed: " & *SDL_GetError()
        delete h : return 0
    end if
    UpdateScale( h )
    if FinishSurface( h ) = false then SDL_DestroyWindow( h->win ) : delete h : return 0
    return h
end function

' A modal dialog window (run it with tkHost_RunModal). w, h in PIXELS. bBorderless for content
' that draws its own caption (tkMessageBox): give it a drag rect with tkHost_SetDragRect.
public function tkHost_CreateDialog( byval owner as TK_HOST ptr, byref title as ustring, _
                                     byval w as long, byval hgt as long, byval bBorderless as boolean = true ) as TK_HOST ptr
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = new TK_HOST
    h->kind = TK_SURF_DIALOG
    h->pOwner = owner
    if owner then
        h->pDefaultFont = owner->pDefaultFont
        h->clrBack = owner->clrBack
        h->fScaleForced = owner->fScaleForced
    end if
    ' Virtual: centred in the base's window, and never larger than it.
    if Virtual_() then
        dim as TK_HOST ptr b = BaseOf_( owner )
        if b then
            dim as long dw = iif( w < b->root->cw, w, b->root->cw ), dh = iif( hgt < b->root->ch, hgt, b->root->ch )
            h->sTitle = title
            if FinishVirtual_( h, b, (b->root->cw - dw) \ 2, (b->root->ch - dh) \ 2, dw, dh ) = false then delete h : return 0
            return h
        end if
    end if
    dim as single d = iif( owner <> 0, owner->fDensity, 1.0 )
    dim as Uint64 fl = SDL_WINDOW_HIGH_PIXEL_DENSITY or SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN
    if bBorderless then fl or= SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS
    dim as string t8 = title
    h->win = SDL_CreateWindow( strptr( t8 ), cint( w / d ), cint( hgt / d ), fl )
    if h->win = 0 then delete h : return 0
    if owner then
        SDL_SetWindowParent( h->win, owner->win )
        if OnTop_( owner ) then SDL_SetWindowAlwaysOnTop( h->win, true )
        ' centre over the owner
        dim as long ox, oy, ow, oh
        SDL_GetWindowPosition( owner->win, @ox, @oy )
        SDL_GetWindowSize( owner->win, @ow, @oh )
        SDL_SetWindowPosition( h->win, ox + (ow - cint( w / d )) \ 2, oy + (oh - cint( hgt / d )) \ 2 )
    end if
    UpdateScale( h )
    if FinishSurface( h ) = false then SDL_DestroyWindow( h->win ) : delete h : return 0
    return h
end function

public function tkHost_Root( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return h->root
end function

public sub tkHost_Show( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if h->bVirtual then
        h->bShown = true
        h->pBase->bDirty = true
    else
        SDL_ShowWindow( h->win )
    end if
    SizeRoot( h )
    h->bDirty = true
end sub

' An owned window (a dialog, a floating palette) about to be hidden or destroyed while it is the
' active one gives activation to its owner FIRST, as tkHost_RunModal does. Hidden while active,
' the OS activates the next window in z-order -- often another application's ("docking a floating
' pane sent tkEdit behind another app", 2026-11-22). Popups and tooltips never take activation.
private sub GiveActivationToOwner_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if (h = 0) orelse (h->win = 0) orelse (h->pOwner = 0) then exit sub
    if h->kind <> TK_SURF_DIALOG then exit sub
    if (h->pOwner->win = 0) orelse (SDL_GetKeyboardFocus() <> h->win) then exit sub
    if (SDL_GetWindowFlags( h->pOwner->win ) and SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN) <> 0 then exit sub
    SDL_RaiseWindow( h->pOwner->win )
end sub

' Hides the window and keeps everything in it. tkHost_Show brings it back.
public sub tkHost_Hide( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if h->bVirtual then
        h->bShown = false
        h->pBase->bDirty = true
    else
        ' master's f643496b3: an owned dialog hidden while active hands activation to its owner first.
        ' Not for a virtual surface: it is a rectangle in its owner's window, never active on its own.
        GiveActivationToOwner_( h )
        SDL_HideWindow( h->win )
    end if
    if h->pOwner then h->pOwner->bDirty = true
end sub

public sub tkHost_PixelSize( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byref w as long, byref hgt as long )
    w = 0 : hgt = 0
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if h->bVirtual then w = h->vw : hgt = h->vh : exit sub
    if Virtual_() andalso (h->root <> 0) then w = h->root->cw : hgt = h->root->ch : exit sub
    SDL_GetRenderOutputSize( h->renderer, @w, @hgt )
end sub

' Where h's pixel 0,0 is in its window's back buffer: 0,0 for a window, the rectangle's corner for
' a virtual surface. What a test reading pixels adds (tkTest).
public sub tkHost_Origin( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byref ox as long, byref oy as long )
    ox = 0 : oy = 0
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if h->bVirtual then
        ox = h->pBase->ix + h->vx : oy = h->pBase->iy + h->vy
    else
        ox = h->ix : oy = h->iy
    end if
end sub

' A surface's size in pixels: a window's (in window coordinates, so divided by its density), or a
' virtual surface's rectangle, which keeps its corner unless it no longer fits in its base.
public sub tkHost_SetPixelSize( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as long, byval hgt as long )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if h->bVirtual = false then
        SDL_SetWindowSize( h->win, cint( w / h->fDensity ), cint( hgt / h->fDensity ) )
        exit sub
    end if
    dim as TK_HOST ptr b = h->pBase
    h->vw = iif( w < b->root->cw, w, b->root->cw ) : h->vh = iif( hgt < b->root->ch, hgt, b->root->ch )
    if h->vx + h->vw > b->root->cw then h->vx = b->root->cw - h->vw
    if h->vy + h->vh > b->root->ch then h->vy = b->root->ch - h->vh
    SizeRoot( h )
    if h->OnSize then h->OnSize( h )
    h->bDirty = true
    b->bDirty = true
end sub

' Is h on screen: a window not hidden, or a virtual surface shown and not closed.
public function tkHost_IsShown( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    if (h = 0) orelse h->bClosed then return false
    if h->bVirtual then return h->bShown
    return (SDL_GetWindowFlags( h->win ) and SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN) = 0
end function

' h's title: its window's, or the one a virtual page was created with.
public function tkHost_GetTitle( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as ustring
    if h = 0 then return ""
    if h->bVirtual then return h->sTitle
    dim as const zstring ptr t = SDL_GetWindowTitle( h->win )
    if t = 0 then return ""
    return *t
end function

' A virtual surface centred in its base (a dialog after it was sized). Nothing for a window.
public sub tkHost_CentreVirtual( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if (h = 0) orelse (h->bVirtual = false) then exit sub
    h->vx = (h->pBase->root->cw - h->vw) \ 2 : h->vy = (h->pBase->root->ch - h->vh) \ 2
    h->pBase->bDirty = true
end sub

' The back buffer's pixels in a rect of h's own pixels (render with tkHost_RenderTo( h, false )
' first): SDL_RenderReadPixels, moved by h's origin -- a virtual surface's place, the safe area's
' corner -- and read with no viewport. A window on the desktop reads exactly what it did.
public function tkHost_ReadPixels( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval rc as const SDL_Rect ptr ) as SDL_Surface ptr
    if (h = 0) orelse (rc = 0) then return 0
    dim as SDL_Rect r = *rc
    dim as long ox, oy
    tkHost_Origin( h, ox, oy )
    r.x += ox : r.y += oy
    if Virtual_() then SDL_SetRenderViewport( h->renderer, 0 )
    return SDL_RenderReadPixels( h->renderer, @r )
end function

' The window id an SDL event addressed to h carries: its own, or a virtual surface's base's.
public function tkHost_WindowId( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as SDL_WindowID
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return h->winId
end function

' A point in h's pixels as an SDL event addressed to h carries it: h's window id and WINDOW
' coordinates (a virtual surface's own id, so the event reaches it directly). What a test pushes.
public sub tkHost_ToWindow( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval px as single, byval py as single, _
                            byref wid as SDL_WindowID, byref wx as single, byref wy as single )
    wid = 0 : wx = px : wy = py
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    wid = h->winId
    if h->bVirtual = false then px += h->ix : py += h->iy
    wx = px / h->fDensity : wy = py / h->fDensity
end sub

public sub tkHost_Invalidate( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h then h->bDirty = true
end sub

' Where a popup of size w x h should go to sit against rcAnchor (OWNER window pixels): below
' it (bSide = false) or to its right (bSide = true), flipped above / to the left when the
' display has no room. On Wayland the window's global position is unknown and reads 0,0, so
' the flip is decided against the display alone and the compositor's positioner does the rest.
public sub tkHost_PlacePopup( byval owner as TK_HOST ptr, byref rcAnchor as TKRECT, byval w as long, byval hgt as long, _
                              byval bSide as boolean, byref x as long, byref y as long )
    x = rcAnchor.left : y = rcAnchor.bottom
    if bSide then x = rcAnchor.right : y = rcAnchor.top
    if owner = 0 then exit sub
    ' VIRTUAL: the room is the base window's, in the owner's pixels; flipped as below, then kept
    ' inside it, since nothing can be drawn outside the one window.
    if Virtual_() then
        dim as TK_HOST ptr b = BaseOf_( owner )
        if b = 0 then exit sub
        dim as long ox = 0, oy = 0
        if owner->bVirtual then ox = owner->vx : oy = owner->vy
        dim as long bw = b->root->cw, bh = b->root->ch
        if bSide then
            if ox + x + w > bw then x = rcAnchor.left - w
            if oy + y + hgt > bh then y = rcAnchor.bottom - hgt
        else
            if oy + y + hgt > bh then y = rcAnchor.top - hgt
            if ox + x + w > bw then x = rcAnchor.right - w
        end if
        if ox + x + w > bw then x = bw - w - ox
        if oy + y + hgt > bh then y = bh - hgt - oy
        if ox + x < 0 then x = -ox
        if oy + y < 0 then y = -oy
        exit sub
    end if
    dim as SDL_Rect rd
    if SDL_GetDisplayUsableBounds( SDL_GetDisplayForWindow( owner->win ), @rd ) = false then exit sub
    dim as long wx, wy
    SDL_GetWindowPosition( owner->win, @wx, @wy )
    dim as single d = owner->fDensity
    ' everything in window coordinates for the comparison
    dim as single gx = wx + x / d, gy = wy + y / d, gw = w / d, gh = hgt / d
    if bSide then
        if gx + gw > rd.x + rd.w then x = rcAnchor.left - w
        if gy + gh > rd.y + rd.h then y = rcAnchor.bottom - hgt
    else
        if gy + gh > rd.y + rd.h then y = rcAnchor.top - hgt
        if gx + gw > rd.x + rd.w then x = rcAnchor.right - w
    end if
end sub


' ---- widget tree -------------------------------------------------------------------------
public function tkWidget_Send( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval m as TK_MSG ptr ) as boolean
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->proc = 0) then return false
    return w->proc( w, m )
end function

private sub SendSimple( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval msg as long, byval pOther as TK_WIDGET ptr = 0 )
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = msg
    m.pOther = pOther
    tkWidget_Send( w, @m )
end sub

' The widget's rect in WINDOW pixels.
public sub tkWidget_AbsRect( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byref rc as TKRECT )
    dim as long ax = 0, ay = 0
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr p = w
    while p
        ax += p->x : ay += p->y
        p = p->pParent
    wend
    tkRect_Set( rc, ax, ay, ax + w->cw, ay + w->ch )
end sub

public function tkWidget_IsEnabled( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as boolean
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr p = w
    while p
        if p->isEnabled = false then return false
        p = p->pParent
    wend
    return w <> 0
end function

public function tkWidget_IsVisible( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as boolean
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr p = w
    while p
        if p->isVisible = false then return false
        p = p->pParent
    wend
    return w <> 0
end function

private sub AppendChild( byval parent as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    w->pParent = parent
    w->pPrev = parent->pLast
    w->pNext = 0
    if parent->pLast then parent->pLast->pNext = w else parent->pFirst = w
    parent->pLast = w
end sub

private sub Unlink( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr parent = w->pParent
    if parent = 0 then exit sub
    if w->pPrev then w->pPrev->pNext = w->pNext else parent->pFirst = w->pNext
    if w->pNext then w->pNext->pPrev = w->pPrev else parent->pLast = w->pPrev
    w->pParent = 0 : w->pNext = 0 : w->pPrev = 0
end sub

' A child of `parent` (a widget, or tkHost_Root for a top-level one), on top of its siblings.
public function tkWidget_CreateChild( byval parent as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval ctrlId as long, _
                                      byval proc as tkWidgetProc, byval pData as any ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if parent = 0 then return 0
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = new TK_WIDGET
    w->pHost  = parent->pHost
    w->ctrlId = ctrlId
    w->proc   = proc
    w->pData  = pData
    AppendChild( parent, w )
    return w
end function

' A top-level widget of the surface (a child of its root).
public function tkWidget_Create( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval ctrlId as long, _
                                 byval proc as tkWidgetProc, byval pData as any ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return tkWidget_CreateChild( h->root, ctrlId, proc, pData )
end function

public function tkWidget_Parent( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if w = 0 then return 0
    return w->pParent
end function

' Move to the top of the sibling z-order.
public sub tkWidget_BringToTop( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->pParent = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr parent = w->pParent
    Unlink( w )
    AppendChild( parent, w )
    w->pHost->bDirty = true
end sub

' Move before `before` in the sibling z-order: below it, and ahead of it in the Tab order. `before`
' = 0 moves to the top. A `before` that is not a sibling leaves the order alone.
public sub tkWidget_MoveBefore( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval before as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->pParent = 0) orelse (w = before) then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr parent = w->pParent
    if before = 0 then
        tkWidget_BringToTop( w )
        exit sub
    end if
    if before->pParent <> parent then exit sub
    Unlink( w )
    w->pParent = parent
    w->pNext = before
    w->pPrev = before->pPrev
    if before->pPrev then before->pPrev->pNext = w else parent->pFirst = w
    before->pPrev = w
    w->pHost->bDirty = true
end sub

' Move to the bottom of the sibling z-order, and first in the Tab order.
public sub tkWidget_SendToBack( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->pParent = 0) then exit sub
    tkWidget_MoveBefore( w, w->pParent->pFirst )
end sub

public sub tkWidget_Invalidate( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if w andalso w->pHost then w->pHost->bDirty = true
end sub

' SetWindowPos, parent-relative. A size change sends TKM_SIZE, as WM_SIZE followed one.
public sub tkWidget_SetPos( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval x as long, byval y as long, byval cw as long, byval ch as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    dim as boolean bSized = (cw <> w->cw) orelse (ch <> w->ch)
    w->x = x : w->y = y : w->cw = cw : w->ch = ch
    if bSized then SendSimple( w, TKM_SIZE )
    tkWidget_Invalidate( w )
end sub

public sub tkWidget_SetSize( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cw as long, byval ch as long )
    if w then tkWidget_SetPos( w, w->x, w->y, cw, ch )
end sub

public function tkHost_GetCapture( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return h->pCapture
end function

' SetCapture. SDL_CaptureMouse is what makes a release OUTSIDE the window arrive; it needs
' mouse focus and is unsupported on Wayland, where the implicit grab during a held button does
' the same job. bCaptureOS records which is in force.
public sub tkHost_SetCapture( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->pHost = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    if h->pCapture = w then exit sub
    if h->pCapture then
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr pOld = h->pCapture
        h->pCapture = 0
        SendSimple( pOld, TKM_CAPTURECHANGED )
    end if
    h->pCapture = w
    h->bCaptureOS = SDL_CaptureMouse( true )
end sub

' ReleaseCapture. Sends TKM_CAPTURECHANGED SYNCHRONOUSLY to the widget losing it, exactly as
' Win32 does -- which is the reason tkButton snapshots its press before releasing.
public sub tkHost_ReleaseCapture( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if (h = 0) orelse (h->pCapture = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr pOld = h->pCapture
    h->pCapture = 0
    if h->bCaptureOS then SDL_CaptureMouse( false )
    h->bCaptureOS = false
    SendSimple( pOld, TKM_CAPTURECHANGED )
end sub

public function tkHost_GetFocus( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return h->pFocus
end function

' THE SOFT KEYBOARD AND WHERE IT LOOKS (A5 step 6). On Android SDL puts a hidden EditText at the
' text input area, and the window is panned until that EditText clears the keyboard (measured: a
' box at the bottom moved up 730 px). A control gives the caret's line, so the pan stopped with
' the rest of the box under the keyboard; with virtual surfaces the area is the whole focused
' widget, and it is set before the keyboard is asked for, so the first pan is the right one.
private sub WholeWidgetArea_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cursorX as long )
    dim as TKRECT a
    tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
    dim as long ox, oy
    tkHost_Origin( h, ox, oy )
    dim as SDL_Rect r
    r.x = cint( (a.left + ox) / h->fDensity ) : r.y = cint( (a.top + oy) / h->fDensity )
    r.w = cint( (a.right - a.left) / h->fDensity ) : r.h = cint( (a.bottom - a.top) / h->fDensity )
    SDL_SetTextInputArea( h->win, @r, cint( cursorX / h->fDensity ) )
end sub

' THE KIND OF KEYBOARD (docs/fasting-android F4 X1): a text widget says what it takes -- a line, a
' multi-line note, a decimal, a whole number, a password -- and the text input is started with
' those properties, so a phone shows a number pad, or a keyboard that does not learn a password.
' SDL has no decimal type: its NUMBER is Android's TYPE_CLASS_NUMBER without the DECIMAL flag
' (measured, F0-FACTS c), so Android's own input type is given as well (0x3002 = NUMBER | SIGNED |
' DECIMAL; 0x1002 NUMBER | SIGNED; 0x81 TEXT | PASSWORD, no autocorrect). TK_TEXT_DEFAULT is SDL's
' own default, as every text widget had before. On a desktop the properties change nothing visible.
private sub StartText_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    dim as long k = 0
    if w then k = w->nTextKind
    h->nTextKindOn = k
    if k = TK_TEXT_DEFAULT then SDL_StartTextInput( h->win ) : exit sub
    dim as SDL_PropertiesID p = SDL_CreateProperties( )
    select case k
    case TK_TEXT_LINE
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER, SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN, false )
    case TK_TEXT_MULTILINE
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER, SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT )
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_CAPITALIZATION_NUMBER, SDL_CAPITALIZE_SENTENCES )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN, true )
    case TK_TEXT_DECIMAL
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER, SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER )
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_ANDROID_INPUTTYPE_NUMBER, &h3002 )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN, false )
    case TK_TEXT_INTEGER
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER, SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER )
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_ANDROID_INPUTTYPE_NUMBER, &h1002 )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN, false )
    case TK_TEXT_PASSWORD
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER, SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_PASSWORD_HIDDEN )
        SDL_SetNumberProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_ANDROID_INPUTTYPE_NUMBER, &h81 )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_AUTOCORRECT_BOOLEAN, false )
        SDL_SetBooleanProperty( p, SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN, false )
    end select
    SDL_StartTextInputWithProperties( h->win, p )
    SDL_DestroyProperties( p )
end sub

' THE KEYBOARD AGAIN: Android ignores the request made while the window is not focused (a field
' focused at start-up got none, measured), and BACK hides it with the field still focused. As an
' Android field does, a tap on the focused text widget -- or the window gaining focus -- asks again.
private sub KeyboardAgain_( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if (h = 0) orelse (h->bTextInput = false) orelse (h->pFocus = 0) then exit sub
    if SDL_HasScreenKeyboardSupport( ) = false then exit sub        ' a desktop: no keyboard to bring back
    if (h->pFocus->bWantsText = false) orelse SDL_ScreenKeyboardShown( h->win ) then exit sub
    WholeWidgetArea_( h, h->pFocus, 0 )
    SDL_StopTextInput( h->win )
    StartText_( h, h->pFocus )
end sub

public declare sub tkWidget_SetTimer( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval id as long, byval ms as long )
public declare sub tkWidget_KillTimer( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval id as long )

private sub UpdateTextInput( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as boolean bWant = (h->pFocus <> 0) andalso h->pFocus->bWantsText
    dim as long k = 0
    if bWant then k = h->pFocus->nTextKind
    ' the same state -- or text input on for a field of the same kind -- needs nothing; a field of
    ' ANOTHER kind restarts it, or the keyboard would stay the previous field's
    if bWant = false then tkWidget_KillTimer( h->root, TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART )    ' a restart still due is moot
    if (bWant = h->bTextInput) andalso ((bWant = false) orelse (k = h->nTextKindOn)) then exit sub
    ' ANOTHER KIND WHILE TYPING: stopped and started again -- but on a phone the start comes
    ' 120 ms later (TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART). Measured on Android (F4): a start straight after the
    ' stop lost to the stop's hide, so every other field got no keyboard at all; and a second
    ' start without a stop is ignored, so the keyboard stayed the previous field's kind.
    if bWant andalso h->bTextInput then
        SDL_StopTextInput( h->win )
        if SDL_HasScreenKeyboardSupport( ) then
            h->nTextKindOn = k
            if Virtual_() then WholeWidgetArea_( h, h->pFocus, 0 )
            tkWidget_SetTimer( h->root, TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART, 120 )
            exit sub
        end if
    end if
    h->bTextInput = bWant
    if bWant andalso Virtual_() then WholeWidgetArea_( h, h->pFocus, 0 )
    if bWant then StartText_( h, h->pFocus ) else SDL_StopTextInput( h->win )
end sub

' A widget's keyboard kind (TK_TEXT_*); a focused one's text input restarts with it.
public sub tkWidget_SetTextKind( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval kind as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    if w->nTextKind = kind then exit sub
    w->nTextKind = kind
    if (w->pHost <> 0) andalso (w->pHost->pFocus = w) then UpdateTextInput( w->pHost )
end sub

public function tkWidget_GetTextKind( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as long
    if w = 0 then return 0
    return w->nTextKind
end function

' What the live text input was started with: -1 when none is on (self-tests).
public function tkHost_TextKindOn( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as long
    if (h = 0) orelse (h->bTextInput = false) then return -1
    return h->nTextKindOn
end function

public sub tkHost_SetFocus( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    if w then
        if (tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) = false) orelse (tkWidget_IsVisible( w ) = false) then exit sub
    end if
    if h->pFocus = w then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr pOld = h->pFocus
    h->pFocus = w
    if pOld then SendSimple( pOld, TKM_KILLFOCUS, w )
    if w then SendSimple( w, TKM_SETFOCUS, pOld )
    UpdateTextInput( h )
end sub

' Where the IME should put its candidate window: rc in widget-local pixels, cursorX the caret's
' offset inside it.
public sub tkHost_SetTextInputArea( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byref rc as TKRECT, byval cursorX as long )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->pHost = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    if Virtual_() then WholeWidgetArea_( h, w, rc.left + cursorX ) : exit sub   ' see UpdateTextInput
    dim as TKRECT a
    tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
    dim as SDL_Rect r
    r.x = cint( (a.left + rc.left) / h->fDensity ) : r.y = cint( (a.top + rc.top) / h->fDensity )
    r.w = cint( (rc.right - rc.left) / h->fDensity ) : r.h = cint( (rc.bottom - rc.top) / h->fDensity )
    dim as long ox, oy
    tkHost_Origin( h, ox, oy )
    r.x += cint( ox / h->fDensity ) : r.y += cint( oy / h->fDensity )
    SDL_SetTextInputArea( h->win, @r, cint( cursorX / h->fDensity ) )
end sub

' Is p the widget w or one of its descendants?
private function IsWithin( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval p as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as boolean
    while p
        if p = w then return true
        p = p->pParent
    wend
    return false
end function

public function tkWidget_IsAncestorOf( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval p as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as boolean
    return (w <> 0) andalso IsWithin( w, p )
end function

private sub SetHostDeep( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    w->pHost = h
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pFirst
    while c
        SetHostDeep( c, h )
        c = c->pNext
    wend
end sub

' msg to every descendant of w (not w itself). A TKM_THEMECHANGED stops at a subtree that carries
' its own theme (pThemeScope): that subtree's theme did not change.
private sub BroadcastTree( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval msg as long )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pFirst
    while c
        if (msg <> TKM_THEMECHANGED) orelse (c->pThemeScope = 0) then
            SendSimple( c, msg )
            BroadcastTree( c, msg )
        end if
        c = c->pNext
    wend
end sub

' msg to w and its whole subtree (tkTheme_ApplyTo's broadcast), with BroadcastTree's scope rule
' below w.
public sub tkWidget_Broadcast( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval msg as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    SendSimple( w, msg )
    BroadcastTree( w, msg )
    if w->pHost then w->pHost->bDirty = true
end sub

' The nearest widget at or above w that carries a theme scope; 0 = the app's theme.
private function ScopeOwner( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    while w
        if w->pThemeScope then return w
        w = w->pParent
    wend
    return 0
end function

' SetParent: move w and its subtree under newParent, on the same surface or another one (a
' dialog recreated at its final size -- on Wayland a surface resized after its renderer exists
' keeps a stale drawable). The old surface forgets any capture, focus or hot widget inside it.
public sub tkWidget_Reparent( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval newParent as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (w = 0) orelse (newParent = 0) orelse (w->pParent = 0) then exit sub
    if IsWithin( w, newParent ) then exit sub                  ' never under itself
    dim as TK_HOST ptr hOld = w->pHost, hNew = newParent->pHost
    if (hOld <> 0) andalso (hOld <> hNew) then
        if IsWithin( w, hOld->pCapture ) then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( hOld )
        if IsWithin( w, hOld->pFocus ) then tkHost_SetFocus( hOld, 0 )
        if IsWithin( w, hOld->pHot ) then hOld->pHot = 0
        if IsWithin( w, hOld->pLastDown ) then hOld->pLastDown = 0
        hOld->bDirty = true
    end if
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr scopeOld = ScopeOwner( w->pParent )
    Unlink( w )
    AppendChild( newParent, w )
    SetHostDeep( w, hNew )
    hNew->bDirty = true
    ' moved between differently themed subtrees: it restyles (a widget with its own scope keeps it)
    if (w->pThemeScope = 0) andalso (ScopeOwner( newParent ) <> scopeOld) then tkWidget_Broadcast( w, TKM_THEMECHANGED )
end sub

' EnableWindow: a disabled widget (and its subtree) gets no input, is skipped by Tab, and gives
' up hot, capture and focus at once rather than at the next event.
public sub tkWidget_Enable( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval bEnable as boolean )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    if w->isEnabled = bEnable then exit sub
    w->isEnabled = bEnable
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    if bEnable = false then
        if IsWithin( w, h->pCapture ) then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pFocus ) then tkHost_SetFocus( h, 0 )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pHot ) then h->pHot = 0
    end if
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = TKM_ENABLE
    m.bFlag = bEnable
    tkWidget_Send( w, @m )
    tkWidget_Invalidate( w )
end sub

public sub tkWidget_Show( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval bShow as boolean )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    if w->isVisible = bShow then exit sub
    w->isVisible = bShow
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    if bShow = false then
        if IsWithin( w, h->pCapture ) then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pFocus ) then tkHost_SetFocus( h, 0 )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pHot ) then h->pHot = 0
    end if
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = TKM_SHOW
    m.bFlag = bShow
    tkWidget_Send( w, @m )
    tkWidget_Invalidate( w )
    if gOnShowChanged then gOnShowChanged( w, bShow )
end sub

' ---- adornments: a child that decorates its parent (an attached badge, a validation mark). It is
' ---- painted right after the parent's own subtree, with the clip the PARENT was given -- so it
' ---- may overhang the parent and sits above it and its other children -- after a TKM_ADORNLAYOUT
' ---- that lets it place itself against the parent's current size. It is never hit-tested (a
' ---- click on it reaches whatever is below), never in the Tab order, and otherwise an ordinary
' ---- child: hidden, moved, rescaled, rethemed and destroyed with its parent. A sibling above the
' ---- parent in z-order covers it as it covers the parent. ----------------------------------------
public sub tkWidget_SetAdorner( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval bOn as boolean )
    if (w = 0) orelse (w->bAdorner = bOn) then exit sub
    w->bAdorner = bOn
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    if bOn andalso (h <> 0) then
        ' it takes no input from now on: let go of whatever input state it held
        if IsWithin( w, h->pCapture ) then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pFocus ) then tkHost_SetFocus( h, 0 )
        if IsWithin( w, h->pHot ) then h->pHot = 0
    end if
    tkWidget_Invalidate( w )
end sub

public function tkWidget_IsAdorner( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as boolean
    return (w <> 0) andalso w->bAdorner
end function

' ---- context menus: a component (tkContextMenu) a right-click or the Menu key opens. The
' ---- release of the right button over w, or over anything inside it, goes to the component as
' ---- TKM_CONTEXTMENU INSTEAD of to the control, so it replaces a control's own menu. --------
public sub tkWidget_SetContextMenu( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval hMenu as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    if (hMenu <> 0) andalso (hMenu->pHost <> w->pHost) then exit sub   ' one surface: it shows there
    w->pContextMenu = hMenu
end sub

public function tkWidget_GetContextMenu( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    return iif( w <> 0, w->pContextMenu, cast( TK_WIDGET ptr, 0 ) )
end function

private sub ClearMenuRefs_( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval hMenu as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if w->pContextMenu = hMenu then w->pContextMenu = 0
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr k = w->pFirst
    while k
        ClearMenuRefs_( k, hMenu )
        k = k->pNext
    wend
end sub

' Every widget of hMenu's surface that has it as its context menu has none: a component calls this
' as it goes, so nothing is left pointing at it.
public sub tkWidget_ClearContextMenuRefs( byval hMenu as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if (hMenu = 0) orelse (hMenu->pHost = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr r = tkHost_Root( hMenu->pHost )
    if r then ClearMenuRefs_( r, hMenu )
end sub

' The first widget from w up its parents with a context menu, 0 for none. A disabled one on the way
' stops the search, as it would have swallowed the click.
private function ContextOwner_( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    while w
        if tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) = false then return 0
        if w->pContextMenu then return w
        w = w->pParent
    wend
    return 0
end function

private sub SendContextMenu_( byval owner as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval x as single, byval y as single, byval bKeyboard as boolean )
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = TKM_CONTEXTMENU
    m.pOther = owner
    m.x = x
    m.y = y
    m.bFlag = bKeyboard
    tkWidget_Send( owner->pContextMenu, @m )
end sub

' Watches the mouse moving over w: over w itself, and over any descendant that has no watcher of
' its own (the nearest one with a watcher is told). Independent of w's own proc; 0 clears it.
public sub tkWidget_SetMouseMoveCallback( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cb as TK_MouseMoveSub )
    if w then w->pOnMouseMove = cb
end sub

' The nearest of w and its ancestors that watches the mouse is told of a move at window pixels px, py.
private sub NotifyMouseMove_( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval px as single, byval py as single, byval buttons as long )
    while (w <> 0) andalso (w->pOnMouseMove = 0)
        w = w->pParent
    wend
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    dim as TKRECT a
    tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
    w->pOnMouseMove( w, cint( px - a.left ), cint( py - a.top ), buttons, clng( SDL_GetModState( ) ) )
end sub

public sub tkWidget_SetCursor( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cursor as long )
    if w then w->cursor = cursor
end sub


' ---- timers: SDL_AddTimer runs its callback on ANOTHER THREAD, so it only pushes an event;
' ---- the tick reaches the widget on the UI thread, as WM_TIMER did. -----------------------
private function TimerTick( byval userdata as any ptr, byval timerID as SDL_TimerID, byval interval as Uint32 ) as Uint32
    dim as TK_TIMER ptr t = cast( TK_TIMER ptr, userdata )
    dim as SDL_Event e
    e.type = gEvTimer
    e.user.code = t->gen
    e.user.data1 = userdata
    SDL_PushEvent( @e )
    return interval
end function

public sub tkWidget_KillTimer( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval id as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gTimers )
        if gTimers(i).active andalso (gTimers(i).pW = w) andalso (gTimers(i).id = id) then
            SDL_RemoveTimer( gTimers(i).sdlId )
            gTimers(i).active = false
            gTimers(i).gen += 1
        end if
    next
end sub

public sub tkWidget_SetTimer( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval id as long, byval ms as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    tkWidget_KillTimer( w, id )
    if gEvTimer = 0 then gEvTimer = SDL_RegisterEvents( 1 )
    ' A fixed pool, never reallocated: SDL holds pointers into it.
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gTimers )
        if gTimers(i).active = false then
            gTimers(i).pW = w
            gTimers(i).id = id
            gTimers(i).active = true
            gTimers(i).sdlId = SDL_AddTimer( iif( ms < 1, 1, ms ), @TimerTick, @gTimers(i) )
            exit sub
        end if
    next
end sub

public function tkWidget_HasTimer( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval id as long ) as boolean
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gTimers )
        if gTimers(i).active andalso (gTimers(i).pW = w) andalso (gTimers(i).id = id) then return true
    next
    return false
end function


' ---- destruction -------------------------------------------------------------------------
public sub tkWidget_Destroy( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    ' children first, so a container's proc can still see its own state while they go
    while w->pLast
        tkWidget_Destroy( w->pLast )
    wend
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = w->pHost
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gTimers )
        if gTimers(i).active andalso (gTimers(i).pW = w) then tkWidget_KillTimer( w, gTimers(i).id )
    next
    if h then
        if h->pCapture = w then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
        if h->pFocus = w then h->pFocus = 0 : UpdateTextInput( h )
        if h->pHot = w then h->pHot = 0
        if h->pLastDown = w then h->pLastDown = 0
        h->bDirty = true
    end if
    SendSimple( w, TKM_DESTROY )
    Unlink( w )
    if w->pThemeScope then deallocate( w->pThemeScope )
    if w->pColorRecipe then deallocate( w->pColorRecipe )
    delete w
end sub

private sub DestroyNow( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    ' popups and dialogs owned by this surface go first
    dim as long i = 0
    while i < gnHosts
        if gHosts(i)->pOwner = h then
            DestroyNow( gHosts(i) )
            i = 0
        else
            i += 1
        end if
    wend
    if h->root then
        while h->root->pLast
            tkWidget_Destroy( h->root->pLast )
        wend
        ' the root's own timers too (the keyboard restart, F4): a tick after this would reach a
        ' freed widget -- measured, a SIGSEGV in tkHost_Dispatch on the next host's pump
        for i as long = 0 to ubound( gTimers )
            if gTimers(i).active andalso (gTimers(i).pW = h->root) then tkWidget_KillTimer( h->root, gTimers(i).id )
        next
        delete h->root
        h->root = 0
    end if
    for k as long = 0 to ubound( h->fonts )
        tkHost_CloseFont( h->fonts(k).f )
    next
    Unregister( h )
    if gMouseHost = h then gMouseHost = 0
    if h->bVirtual then
        if h->pBase then h->pBase->bDirty = true
        delete h
        exit sub
    end if
    if h->engine then TTF_DestroyRendererTextEngine( h->engine )
    if h->renderer then
        if gOnRendererGone then gOnRendererGone( h->renderer )
        SDL_DestroyRenderer( h->renderer )
    end if
    if h->win then SDL_DestroyWindow( h->win )
    delete h
end sub

' Close a popup or dialog: hidden at once, OnClosed fired, and the window destroyed after the
' event being dispatched has finished -- a widget proc inside the popup may be the caller.
public sub tkHost_Close( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if (h = 0) orelse h->bClosed then exit sub
    ' close its own popups first (a submenu chain closes from the leaf)
    for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
        if (i < gnHosts) andalso (gHosts(i)->pOwner = h) andalso (gHosts(i)->kind <> TK_SURF_DIALOG) then tkHost_Close( gHosts(i) )
    next
    h->bClosed = true
    if h->pCapture then tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
    if h->bVirtual then
        h->bShown = false
        h->pBase->bDirty = true
    else
        ' master's f643496b3: an owned dialog hidden while active hands activation to its owner first.
        ' Not for a virtual surface: it is a rectangle in its owner's window, never active on its own.
        GiveActivationToOwner_( h )
        SDL_HideWindow( h->win )
    end if
    if h->pOwner then h->pOwner->bDirty = true
    if h->OnClosed then h->OnClosed( h )
end sub

public function tkHost_IsOpen( byval h as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    if h = 0 then return false
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if gHosts(i) = h then return (h->bClosed = false)
    next
    return false
end function

' Destroy every surface that was closed. Called by the pump between events. A pump nested inside a
' delivery (a menu command waiting on a file dialog) leaves them to the outermost one: the surface
' that delivery came through is still in use when the handler returns.
public sub tkHost_Reap()
    if gDispatching > 0 then exit sub
    dim as long i = 0
    while i < gnHosts
        if gHosts(i)->bClosed then
            DestroyNow( gHosts(i) )
            i = 0
        else
            i += 1
        end if
    wend
end sub

public sub tkHost_Destroy( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    tkHost_Close( h )
    DestroyNow( h )
end sub


' ---- painting ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' One widget at window pixels (cx, cy), then its children, inside rcClip.
private sub PaintOne( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval c as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cx as long, byval cy as long, _
                      byref rcClip as TKRECT )
    dim as TK_PAINT wp
    wp.renderer = h->renderer
    wp.engine = h->engine
    wp.pFont = h->pDefaultFont
    wp.fScale = h->fScale
    wp.Begin( cx, cy, c->cw, c->ch, @rcClip )
    if tkRect_IsEmpty( wp.rcClip ) then exit sub
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = TKM_PAINT
    m.pPaint = @wp
    tkWidget_Send( c, @m )
    if c->pFirst then
        dim as TKRECT rcKids = rcClip
        if c->bClipChildren then rcKids = wp.rcClip
        PaintTree( h, c, cx, cy, rcKids )
    end if
end sub

' c's adornments, after c's own subtree: placed (TKM_ADORNLAYOUT) against c as it is now, then
' painted with the clip c itself was given, so they may overhang c and sit above it and its children.
private sub PaintAdornments( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval c as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval cx as long, byval cy as long, _
                             byref rcClip as TKRECT )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr a = c->pFirst
    while a
        if a->bAdorner andalso a->isVisible then
            dim as boolean bWasDirty = h->bDirty
            SendSimple( a, TKM_ADORNLAYOUT )
            h->bDirty = bWasDirty                ' this frame paints the new rect already
            if (a->cw > 0) andalso (a->ch > 0) then PaintOne( h, a, cx + a->x, cy + a->y, rcClip )
        end if
        a = a->pNext
    wend
end sub

private sub PaintTree( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval ax as long, byval ay as long, _
                       byref rcClip as TKRECT )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pFirst
    while c
        ' an adornment is painted by its target's turn (PaintAdornments), never in the child order
        if (c->bAdorner = false) andalso c->isVisible andalso (c->cw > 0) andalso (c->ch > 0) then
            dim as long cx = ax + c->x, cy = ay + c->y
            PaintOne( h, c, cx, cy, rcClip )
            PaintAdornments( h, c, cx, cy, rcClip )
        end if
        c = c->pNext
    wend
end sub

' Paint the whole surface into the back buffer; present it when bPresent. Reading pixels for a
' test means NOT presenting first -- the back buffer is undefined after a present.
' One virtual surface over its base, already painted: its rectangle is the viewport, so its
' tree and OnPaint draw in its own pixels and are clipped to it.
private sub PaintVirtual_( byval v as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as SDL_Rect vr = ( v->pBase->ix + v->vx, v->pBase->iy + v->vy, v->vw, v->vh )
    SDL_SetRenderViewport( v->renderer, @vr )
    SDL_SetRenderClipRect( v->renderer, 0 )
    v->root->cw = v->vw : v->root->ch = v->vh
    SDL_SetRenderDrawColor( v->renderer, (v->clrBack shr 16) and 255, (v->clrBack shr 8) and 255, v->clrBack and 255, (v->clrBack shr 24) and 255 )
    dim as SDL_FRect fr = ( 0, 0, v->vw, v->vh )
    SDL_RenderFillRect( v->renderer, @fr )
    dim as TK_PAINT p
    p.renderer = v->renderer
    p.engine = v->engine
    p.pFont = v->pDefaultFont
    p.fScale = v->fScale
    p.Begin( 0, 0, v->vw, v->vh )
    if v->OnPaint then v->OnPaint( v, @p )
    dim as TKRECT rcAll
    tkRect_Set( rcAll, 0, 0, v->vw, v->vh )
    PaintTree( v, v->root, 0, 0, rcAll )
    SDL_SetRenderClipRect( v->renderer, 0 )
    v->bDirty = false
end sub

public sub tkHost_RenderTo( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval bPresent as boolean )
    if (h = 0) orelse h->bClosed then exit sub
    ' A virtual surface is painted as part of its base. Not presenting leaves the viewport on it,
    ' so SDL_RenderReadPixels reads ITS pixels (SDL3 reads relative to the viewport), as a test
    ' reading a popup's window did.
    if h->bVirtual then
        tkHost_RenderTo( h->pBase, bPresent )
        ' a render to READ a surface that is not shown yet paints it anyway, as a hidden window's
        ' back buffer is painted on the desktop (a test measuring a box before it is run)
        if (bPresent = false) andalso (h->bShown = false) then PaintVirtual_( h )
        if bPresent = false then
            dim as SDL_Rect vr = ( h->pBase->ix + h->vx, h->pBase->iy + h->vy, h->vw, h->vh )
            SDL_SetRenderViewport( h->renderer, @vr )
        end if
        h->bDirty = false
        exit sub
    end if
    h->bDirty = false
    if Virtual_() then SDL_SetRenderViewport( h->renderer, 0 )   ' a read of a virtual surface left it on that
    dim as long pw, ph
    tkHost_PixelSize( h, pw, ph )
    h->root->cw = pw : h->root->ch = ph
    SDL_SetRenderClipRect( h->renderer, 0 )
    ' The clear honours clrBack's ALPHA: a transparent surface (a rounded tooltip) clears to 0.
    SDL_SetRenderDrawColor( h->renderer, (h->clrBack shr 16) and 255, (h->clrBack shr 8) and 255, h->clrBack and 255, (h->clrBack shr 24) and 255 )
    SDL_RenderClear( h->renderer )
    if Virtual_() andalso ((h->ix <> 0) orelse (h->iy <> 0)) then
        dim as SDL_Rect sr = ( h->ix, h->iy, pw, ph )
        SDL_SetRenderViewport( h->renderer, @sr )
    end if
    dim as TK_PAINT p
    p.renderer = h->renderer
    p.engine = h->engine
    p.pFont = h->pDefaultFont
    p.fScale = h->fScale
    p.Begin( 0, 0, pw, ph )
    if h->OnPaint then h->OnPaint( h, @p )
    dim as TKRECT rcAll
    tkRect_Set( rcAll, 0, 0, pw, ph )
    PaintTree( h, h->root, 0, 0, rcAll )
    SDL_SetRenderClipRect( h->renderer, 0 )
    ' the virtual surfaces over it, in creation order: a submenu after its menu
    if Virtual_() then
        for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
            dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
            if v->bVirtual andalso (v->pBase = h) andalso v->bShown andalso (v->bClosed = false) then PaintVirtual_( v )
        next
        SDL_SetRenderViewport( h->renderer, 0 )
    end if
    if bPresent then
        SDL_RenderPresent( h->renderer )
        h->nFrames += 1
        ' The first present after a return to the foreground is never shown (see ResumeWatch):
        ' paint and present once more.
        if h->bResumed then h->bResumed = false : tkHost_RenderTo( h, true )
    end if
end sub

' The whole surface, every time it is dirty. There are no damage regions -- see FINDINGS.
public sub tkHost_Render( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    tkHost_RenderTo( h, true )
end sub

' BACK IN THE FOREGROUND (Android). HOME destroys the Activity's surface; on the return SDL makes a
' new one and restores the GL context, and the window comes back RESTORED -- but no EXPOSED, so
' nothing was dirty and the window stayed black until something repainted. Worse, the first
' SDL_RenderPresent after the return is never shown: a plain SDL program that presents once per
' tap shows black for the first tap and the right frame from the second, with no lag after it
' (measured, API 36 emulator, SDL 3.4.14, 2026-11-25). So every window is dirty again AND its
' next render presents twice. SDL only calls watchers for this event (it is never queued); the
' RESTORED it sends next wakes the loop that renders, after the renderer stops counting the
' window hidden. Main thread only, as below.
private function ResumeWatch( byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean
    if SDL_IsMainThread( ) = false then return true
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        dim as TK_HOST ptr h = gHosts(i)
        if (h->bVirtual = false) andalso (h->bClosed = false) then h->bDirty = true : h->bResumed = true
    next
    return true
end function

' LIVE RESIZE. While a window edge is dragged, Windows runs its own loop: the application's loop
' sees no event until the drag ends, so the window's contents kept their old layout until then.
' SDL3 still calls event WATCHERS from inside that loop, with an SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_EXPOSED whose
' data1 is 1 ("live-resize expose", SDL_events.h): this one lays the host out and paints it there
' and then. Every other event is left to the loop -- the RESIZED it also queued is handled again
' when the drag ends, which costs one layout. Main thread only: a watcher also sees events pushed
' from other threads (tkFileDialog's answer).
function LiveResizeWatch( byval userdata as any ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean
    if e->type = SDL_EVENT_DID_ENTER_FOREGROUND then return ResumeWatch( e )
    if (e->type <> SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_EXPOSED) orelse (e->window.data1 <> 1) then return true
    if SDL_IsMainThread( ) = false then return true
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = HostOfWindow( e->window.windowID )
    if (h = 0) orelse h->bClosed then return true
    SizeRoot( h )
    if h->OnSize then h->OnSize( h )
    RunSizeHooks_( h )
    tkHost_Render( h )
    return true
end function


' ---- input dispatch ----------------------------------------------------------------------
' The deepest visible widget under (px, py) window pixels; children are tested last-to-first,
' so the top of the z-order wins, and a clipping parent prunes children outside it.
private function HitIn( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval px as single, byval py as single, _
                        byval ax as long, byval ay as long ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pLast
    while c
        if c->isVisible andalso (c->bAdorner = false) then     ' an adornment is never hit
            dim as long cx = ax + c->x, cy = ay + c->y
            dim as boolean bIn = (px >= cx) andalso (px < cx + c->cw) andalso (py >= cy) andalso (py < cy + c->ch)
            if bIn orelse (c->bClipChildren = false) then
                dim as TK_WIDGET ptr d = HitIn( c, px, py, cx, cy )
                if d then return d
            end if
            if bIn then return c
        end if
        c = c->pPrev
    wend
    return 0
end function

public function tkHost_HitTest( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval px as single, byval py as single ) as TK_WIDGET ptr
    if h = 0 then return 0
    return HitIn( h->root, px, py, 0, 0 )
end function

private sub SendMouse( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval msg as long, byval px as single, byval py as single, _
                       byval clicks as long = 0 )
    dim as TKRECT a
    tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = msg
    m.x = px - a.left
    m.y = py - a.top
    m.clicks = clicks
    tkWidget_Send( w, @m )
end sub

' The hot widget changes: the old one is told it was left, the new one that it was entered.
' This is the WM_MOUSELEAVE Win32 only delivered to a window that asked -- and not reliably.
private sub SetHot( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr )
    if h->pHot = w then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr pOld = h->pHot
    h->pHot = w
    if pOld then SendSimple( pOld, TKM_MOUSELEAVE )
    if w andalso tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then SendSimple( w, TKM_MOUSEENTER )
    if gOnHotChanged then gOnHotChanged( h, w )
end sub

private sub SyncCursor( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = h->pCapture
    if w = 0 then w = h->pHot
    dim as long c = TK_CURSOR_ARROW
    if w andalso tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then c = w->cursor
    if c = gCursorNow then exit sub
    if gCursors(c) = 0 then
        dim as SDL_SystemCursor sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_DEFAULT
        select case c
        case TK_CURSOR_IBEAM   : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_TEXT
        case TK_CURSOR_HAND    : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_POINTER
        case TK_CURSOR_SIZEWE  : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_EW_RESIZE
        case TK_CURSOR_SIZENS  : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_NS_RESIZE
        case TK_CURSOR_SIZEALL : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_MOVE
        case TK_CURSOR_WAIT    : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_WAIT
        case TK_CURSOR_SIZENWSE : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_NWSE_RESIZE
        case TK_CURSOR_SIZENESW : sc = SDL_SYSTEM_CURSOR_NESW_RESIZE
        end select
        gCursors(c) = SDL_CreateSystemCursor( sc )
    end if
    if gCursors(c) then SDL_SetCursor( gCursors(c) )
    gCursorNow = c
end sub

' Send msg to every widget of every live surface (what PsRegistry's broadcasts did). Used for
' TKM_THEMECHANGED; clrWindow, when non-zero, becomes the background of the main windows and
' dialogs (a popup keeps its own).
public sub tkHost_BroadcastAll( byval msg as long, byval clrWindow as ulong = 0 )
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        dim as TK_HOST ptr h = gHosts(i)
        if h->bClosed then continue for
        if (msg = TKM_THEMECHANGED) andalso (h->root->pThemeScope <> 0) then continue for   ' its own theme
        if (clrWindow <> 0) andalso ((h->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN) orelse (h->kind = TK_SURF_DIALOG)) then h->clrBack = clrWindow
        BroadcastTree( h->root, msg )
        h->bDirty = true
    next
end sub

' The TK_CURSOR_* last applied (-1 before the first pointer event).
public function tkHost_CurrentCursor() as long
    return gCursorNow
end function

' Tab order = tree pre-order over focusable, enabled, visible widgets.
' Tab order: a widget's children by their tab index (tkWidget_SetTabIndex), those without one after
' them in tree (z) order; each child's own children right after it.
private sub CollectFocusable( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, list() as TK_WIDGET ptr, byref n as long )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr kids()
    dim as long nk = 0
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pFirst
    while c
        nk += 1
        c = c->pNext
    wend
    if nk = 0 then exit sub
    redim kids( 0 to nk - 1 )
    nk = 0
    c = w->pFirst
    while c
        kids( nk ) = c : nk += 1
        c = c->pNext
    wend
    ' stable: an insertion sort on (the index, or none last)
    for i as long = 1 to nk - 1
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr k = kids( i )
        dim as long kk = iif( k->nTabIndex > 0, k->nTabIndex, &h7FFFFFFF ), j = i - 1
        while (j >= 0) andalso (iif( kids( j )->nTabIndex > 0, kids( j )->nTabIndex, &h7FFFFFFF ) > kk)
            kids( j + 1 ) = kids( j )
            j -= 1
        wend
        kids( j + 1 ) = k
    next
    for i as long = 0 to nk - 1
        c = kids( i )
        if c->isVisible andalso c->isEnabled andalso (c->bAdorner = false) then
            if c->isFocusable andalso (n <= ubound( list )) then list(n) = c : n += 1
            CollectFocusable( c, list(), n )
        end if
    next
end sub

' A widget's place among its siblings in Tab order (1 first); 0 takes it out of the numbering, after
' the numbered ones in tree order. Its own focusable children follow it either way.
public sub tkWidget_SetTabIndex( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval nIndex as long )
    if w = 0 then exit sub
    w->nTabIndex = iif( nIndex < 0, 0, nIndex )
end sub

public function tkWidget_GetTabIndex( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr ) as long
    if w = 0 then return 0
    return w->nTabIndex
end function

public sub tkHost_FocusNext( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval bBack as boolean = false )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr list(0 to 1023)
    dim as long n = 0
    CollectFocusable( h->root, list(), n )
    if n = 0 then exit sub
    dim as long cur = -1
    for i as long = 0 to n - 1
        if list(i) = h->pFocus then cur = i : exit for
    next
    dim as long nxt
    if bBack then
        nxt = iif( cur < 0, n - 1, (cur - 1 + n) mod n )
    else
        nxt = iif( cur < 0, 0, (cur + 1) mod n )
    end if
    tkHost_SetFocus( h, list(nxt) )
end sub

private sub RescaleTree( byval w as TK_WIDGET ptr, byval fOld as single, byval fNew as single )
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr c = w->pFirst
    while c
        dim as TK_MSG m
        m.msg = TKM_SCALECHANGED
        m.fOld = fOld
        m.fNew = fNew
        tkWidget_Send( c, @m )
        RescaleTree( c, fOld, fNew )
        c = c->pNext
    wend
end sub

private sub RescaleAll( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as single fOld = h->fScale
    UpdateScale( h )
    if fOld = h->fScale then exit sub
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( h->fonts )
        SizeFont( h, h->fonts(i).f, h->fonts(i).pt )
    next
    RescaleTree( h->root, fOld, h->fScale )
    if h->OnScale then h->OnScale( h )
    if h->OnSize then h->OnSize( h )
    RunSizeHooks_( h )
    h->bDirty = true
end sub

' The usable work area of the display h is on, in h's WINDOW PIXELS (so it compares directly
' with anchor rects there). On Wayland the window's global position is unknowable: the area is
' unbounded and the compositor's popup positioner keeps popups on screen.
public sub tkHost_WorkRect( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byref rc as TKRECT )
    tkRect_Set( rc, -1000000, -1000000, 1000000, 1000000 )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    ' virtual: the base window, in h's pixels -- nothing can be drawn outside it
    if Virtual_() then
        dim as TK_HOST ptr b = BaseOf_( h )
        if h->bVirtual = false then b = h
        if b then tkRect_Set( rc, iif( h->bVirtual, -h->vx, 0 ), iif( h->bVirtual, -h->vy, 0 ), _
                              b->root->cw - iif( h->bVirtual, h->vx, 0 ), b->root->ch - iif( h->bVirtual, h->vy, 0 ) )
        exit sub
    end if
    if *SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver() = "wayland" then exit sub
    dim as SDL_Rect rd
    if SDL_GetDisplayUsableBounds( SDL_GetDisplayForWindow( h->win ), @rd ) = false then exit sub
    dim as long wx, wy
    SDL_GetWindowPosition( h->win, @wx, @wy )
    dim as single d = h->fDensity
    tkRect_Set( rc, cint( (rd.x - wx) * d ), cint( (rd.y - wy) * d ), cint( (rd.x + rd.w - wx) * d ), cint( (rd.y + rd.h - wy) * d ) )
end sub

' The open dismissable popup on top, if any.
private function TopPopup() as TK_HOST ptr
    for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
        if (gHosts(i)->kind = TK_SURF_POPUP) andalso (gHosts(i)->bClosed = false) then return gHosts(i)
    next
    return 0
end function

' Is `h` the popup p, or a popup owned (transitively) by p? A press inside a submenu must not
' close the menu it hangs from.
private function InChainOf( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval p as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    while h
        if h = p then return true
        h = h->pOwner
    wend
    return false
end function

' THE DISMISSAL RULE (PsPopupHost's): a press anywhere that is not inside a popup's own chain
' closes that popup, and the press is CONSUMED when it landed outside every popup -- letting the
' dismissing click through would also activate whatever it landed on.
private function DismissFor( byval target as TK_HOST ptr, byval bFocusLoss as boolean = false ) as boolean
    dim as boolean bClosedAny = false
    for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
        if i >= gnHosts then continue for
        dim as TK_HOST ptr p = gHosts(i)
        if bFocusLoss andalso p->bKeepOnFocusLoss then continue for
        if (p->kind = TK_SURF_POPUP) andalso (p->bClosed = false) then
            if InChainOf( target, p ) = false then
                ' a popup that lets its dismissing click through does not make it consumed
                if p->bPassDismissClick = false then bClosedAny = true
                tkHost_Close( p )
            end if
        end if
    next
    return bClosedAny andalso ((target = 0) orelse (target->kind <> TK_SURF_POPUP))
end function

' One-shot (returns 0): post the deferred "did focus leave the application?" check.
private function FocusCheckTick( byval userdata as any ptr, byval timerID as SDL_TimerID, byval interval as Uint32 ) as Uint32
    dim as SDL_Event e
    e.type = gEvFocusCheck
    SDL_PushEvent( @e )
    return 0
end function

private sub FocusCheck()
    dim as SDL_Window ptr kf = SDL_GetKeyboardFocus()
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if gHosts(i)->win = kf then exit sub
    next
    DismissFor( 0, true )
end sub

private sub DispatchKey( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr )
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = iif( e->type = SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, TKM_KEYDOWN, TKM_KEYUP )
    m.key = e->key.key
    m.mods = e->key.mod_
    m.bFlag = e->key.repeat
    m.scancode = e->key.scancode
    ' A gesture in flight hears Escape first, whoever has the focus: a widget that never takes
    ' focus (a column header mid-drag) must still be able to cancel. Win32 controls polled
    ' VK_ESCAPE for this; here the key goes to the capture, then on as usual if refused.
    if (m.msg = TKM_KEYDOWN) andalso (m.key = SDLK_ESCAPE) andalso (h->pCapture <> 0) andalso (h->pCapture <> h->pFocus) then
        if tkWidget_IsEnabled( h->pCapture ) andalso tkWidget_Send( h->pCapture, @m ) then exit sub
    end if
    ' ACCELERATORS FIRST, as TranslateAccelerator ran before a window's own WM_KEYDOWN: an
    ' application's Ctrl+S is the application's whichever control has the focus. Per surface,
    ' so a dialog or a popup (which has none) never runs the main window's commands.
    if (m.msg = TKM_KEYDOWN) andalso (h->OnPreKey <> 0) then
        if h->OnPreKey( h, @m ) then exit sub
    end if
    ' the Menu key or Shift+F10 opens the focused widget's context menu (its own or a parent's),
    ' below it, before the control itself would open one
    if (m.msg = TKM_KEYDOWN) andalso ((m.key = SDLK_APPLICATION) orelse ((m.key = SDLK_F10) andalso ((m.mods and SDL_KMOD_SHIFT) <> 0))) then
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr owner = ContextOwner_( h->pFocus )
        if owner then
            dim as TKRECT a
            tkWidget_AbsRect( h->pFocus, a )
            SendContextMenu_( owner, a.left, a.bottom, true )
            exit sub
        end if
    end if
    ' to the focused widget, bubbling up the parents while refused
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = h->pFocus
    while w
        if tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) andalso tkWidget_Send( w, @m ) then exit sub
        w = w->pParent
    wend
    if m.msg <> TKM_KEYDOWN then exit sub
    ' unclaimed keys: Tab moves focus (the dialog manager's job), Escape closes a popup
    if e->key.key = SDLK_TAB then
        tkHost_FocusNext( h, (e->key.mod_ and SDL_KMOD_SHIFT) <> 0 )
    elseif (e->key.key = SDLK_ESCAPE) andalso (h->kind = TK_SURF_POPUP) then
        tkHost_Close( h )
    end if
end sub

private sub DispatchText( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval msg as long, byref s as string, _
                          byval nStart as long = 0, byval nLen as long = 0 )
    dim as TK_MSG m
    m.msg = msg
    m.text = s
    m.nStart = nStart
    m.nLen = nLen
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = h->pFocus
    if w andalso tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then tkWidget_Send( w, @m )
end sub

private sub DispatchDrop( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval px as single, byval py as single )
    dim as boolean bFiles = (h->nDropFiles > 0)
    if (bFiles = false) andalso (len( h->sDropText ) = 0) then exit sub
    dim as TK_MSG m
    if bFiles then
        m.msg = TKM_DROPFILES : m.text = h->sDropFiles
    else
        m.msg = TKM_DROPTEXT : m.text = h->sDropText
    end if
    m.nStart = h->nDropFiles
    h->sDropFiles = "" : h->nDropFiles = 0 : h->sDropText = ""
    dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py )
    while w
        if tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then
            dim as TKRECT a
            tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
            m.x = px - a.left : m.y = py - a.top
            if tkWidget_Send( w, @m ) then exit sub
        end if
        w = w->pParent
    wend
    m.x = px : m.y = py
    if h->OnDrop then h->OnDrop( h, @m )
end sub

private sub DispatchTo( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr )
    select case e->type
    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_CLOSE_REQUESTED
        if h->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN then
            ' OnCloseRequest may veto a main window's close too (TRUE = handled, stay open)
            if h->OnCloseRequest then
                if h->OnCloseRequest( h ) = false then h->bQuit = true
            else
                h->bQuit = true
            end if
        elseif h->OnCloseRequest then
            if h->OnCloseRequest( h ) = false then h->bEndModal = true : h->nModalResult = 0
        else
            h->bEndModal = true : h->nModalResult = 0
        end if

    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_EXPOSED
        h->bDirty = true

    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED, SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED
        SizeRoot( h )
        if h->OnSize then h->OnSize( h )
        RunSizeHooks_( h )
        h->bDirty = true

    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_DISPLAY_SCALE_CHANGED
        RescaleAll( h )

    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MOUSE_LEAVE
        ' During capture the cursor is allowed to leave; the widget keeps getting moves.
        if h->pCapture = 0 then SetHot( h, 0 )

    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_FOCUS_LOST
        ' Deactivated: capture is gone (Win32 sends WM_CAPTURECHANGED here). Popups close only
        ' when focus left the APPLICATION -- a popup taking focus is not that.
        '
        ' NOT DECIDED NOW. Mapping a popup on Wayland can report the main window's focus lost
        ' while keyboard focus is momentarily nobody's -- dismissing on that closed a menu chain
        ' the instant its submenu opened (measured: 1 Wayland run in 4). The check runs 150 ms
        ' later, when focus has landed somewhere real.
        tkHost_ReleaseCapture( h )
        if gEvFocusCheck = 0 then gEvFocusCheck = SDL_RegisterEvents( 1 )
        SDL_AddTimer( 150, @FocusCheckTick, 0 )

    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION
        dim as single px = e->motion.x * h->fDensity, py = e->motion.y * h->fDensity
        h->lastX = px : h->lastY = py
        if h->pCapture then
            SendMouse( h->pCapture, TKM_MOUSEMOVE, px, py )
        else
            dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py )
            SetHot( h, w )
            if w andalso tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then SendMouse( w, TKM_MOUSEMOVE, px, py )
        end if
        ' the watchers, after the widget itself; looked up again, since the delivery may have
        ' destroyed what was there (a disabled widget still passes the move on to its parents)
        if h->pCapture then
            NotifyMouseMove_( h->pCapture, px, py, clng( e->motion.state ) )
        else
            NotifyMouseMove_( tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py ), px, py, clng( e->motion.state ) )
        end if
        SyncCursor( h )

    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP
        dim as single px = e->button.x * h->fDensity, py = e->button.y * h->fDensity
        h->lastX = px : h->lastY = py
        dim as boolean bDown = (e->type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN)
        dim as long msg
        select case e->button.button
        case SDL_BUTTON_LEFT
            msg = iif( bDown, TKM_LBUTTONDOWN, TKM_LBUTTONUP )
        case SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT
            msg = iif( bDown, TKM_RBUTTONDOWN, TKM_RBUTTONUP )
        case SDL_BUTTON_MIDDLE
            msg = iif( bDown, TKM_MBUTTONDOWN, TKM_MBUTTONUP )
        case else
            exit select
        end select
        ' A press on a dialog's drag band moves the window (SDL_SetWindowHitTest does it);
        ' never seen here when the hit test claimed it.
        dim as long bit = iif( msg = TKM_LBUTTONDOWN orelse msg = TKM_LBUTTONUP, 1, iif( msg = TKM_RBUTTONDOWN orelse msg = TKM_RBUTTONUP, 2, 4 ) )
        if bDown then h->buttonsDown or= bit else h->buttonsDown and= not bit
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = h->pCapture
        if w = 0 then w = tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py )
        dim as long clicks = e->button.clicks
        if bDown then
            ' a double click that changed widgets is two single clicks (PsDispatch's rule)
            if (clicks >= 2) andalso (w <> h->pLastDown) then clicks = 1
            h->pLastDown = w
        end if
        ' A disabled widget swallows the click: it reaches neither it nor anything beneath.
        if w andalso tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then
            ' the right button's release over a widget with a context menu (its own or a parent's)
            ' opens that menu instead of reaching the control
            dim as TK_WIDGET ptr owner = 0
            if (msg = TKM_RBUTTONUP) andalso (h->pCapture = 0) then owner = ContextOwner_( w )
            if owner then
                SendContextMenu_( owner, px, py, false )
            else
                SendMouse( w, msg, px, py, clicks )
            end if
        end if
        SyncCursor( h )

    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL
        dim as single px = e->wheel.mouse_x * h->fDensity, py = e->wheel.mouse_y * h->fDensity
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = h->pCapture
        if w = 0 then w = tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py )
        dim as single dx = e->wheel.x, dy = e->wheel.y
        if e->wheel.direction = SDL_MOUSEWHEEL_FLIPPED then dx = -dx : dy = -dy
        ' up the parents while refused, as DefWindowProc forwards WM_MOUSEWHEEL
        while w
            if tkWidget_IsEnabled( w ) then
                dim as TKRECT a
                tkWidget_AbsRect( w, a )
                dim as TK_MSG m
                m.msg = TKM_MOUSEWHEEL
                m.x = px - a.left : m.y = py - a.top
                m.wheelX = dx : m.wheelY = dy
                m.mods = SDL_GetModState()
                if tkWidget_Send( w, @m ) then exit while
            end if
            w = w->pParent
        wend

    case SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_KEY_UP
        DispatchKey( h, e )

    case SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT
        dim as string s = *e->text.text
        DispatchText( h, TKM_CHAR, s )

    ' A DROP FROM THE OS: SDL sends BEGIN, one FILE or TEXT per item, then COMPLETE with the
    ' point. Collected here and delivered ONCE, on COMPLETE, to the widget under the point --
    ' WM_DROPFILES' shape: one message, every path -- bubbling up the parents while refused,
    ' then to the surface's OnDrop.
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_BEGIN
        h->sDropFiles = "" : h->nDropFiles = 0 : h->sDropText = ""
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_FILE
        if e->drop.data then
            if h->nDropFiles then h->sDropFiles &= chr( 10 )
            h->sDropFiles &= *e->drop.data
            h->nDropFiles += 1
        end if
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_TEXT
        if e->drop.data then h->sDropText &= *e->drop.data
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_COMPLETE
        DispatchDrop( h, e->drop.x * h->fDensity, e->drop.y * h->fDensity )

    case SDL_EVENT_TEXT_EDITING
        dim as string s = ""
        if e->edit.text then s = *e->edit.text
        DispatchText( h, TKM_IMECOMPOSE, s, e->edit.start, e->edit.length )
    end select
end sub

private function EventWindow( byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as SDL_WindowID
    select case e->type
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_FILE to SDL_EVENT_DROP_POSITION : return e->drop.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION : return e->motion.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP : return e->button.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL : return e->wheel.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_KEY_UP : return e->key.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT : return e->text.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_TEXT_EDITING : return e->edit.windowID
    case SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_FIRST to SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_LAST : return e->window.windowID
    end select
    return 0
end function

' Is v an open, shown virtual surface of base?
private function LiveVirtual_( byval v as TK_HOST ptr, byval base_ as TK_HOST ptr ) as boolean
    return v->bVirtual andalso (v->pBase = base_) andalso v->bShown andalso (v->bClosed = false)
end function

' THE VIRTUAL ROUTER: which surface an event that SDL addressed to base's window belongs to, and
' the event as that surface would have received it (`ev`, coordinates in its own window space).
'   pointer   the surface holding the capture; else the topmost live virtual surface under the
'             point (a tooltip takes no input); else the topmost modal one -- a dialog or a page
'             -- when the point is outside it (the modal loop then drops it); else base
'   keys      the top popup (the dispatcher's own rule, after this); else the topmost dialog or
'             page; else base
'   the rest  base (window events, drops begun)
private function VirtualTarget_( byval base_ as TK_HOST ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr, byref ev as SDL_Event ) as TK_HOST ptr
    ev = *e
    dim as single wx, wy
    dim as boolean bPointer = true
    select case e->type
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION : wx = e->motion.x : wy = e->motion.y
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP : wx = e->button.x : wy = e->button.y
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL : wx = e->wheel.mouse_x : wy = e->wheel.mouse_y
    case SDL_EVENT_DROP_COMPLETE : wx = e->drop.x : wy = e->drop.y
    case SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_KEY_UP, SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT, SDL_EVENT_TEXT_EDITING
        bPointer = false
        for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
            dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
            if LiveVirtual_( v, base_ ) andalso ((v->kind = TK_SURF_DIALOG) orelse (v->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN)) then return v
        next
        return base_
    case else
        return base_
    end select
    dim as TK_HOST ptr t = 0
    if base_->pCapture = 0 then
        for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
            dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
            if LiveVirtual_( v, base_ ) andalso (v->pCapture <> 0) then t = v : exit for
        next
    end if
    if t = 0 andalso (base_->pCapture = 0) then
        dim as single px = wx * base_->fDensity - base_->ix, py = wy * base_->fDensity - base_->iy
        for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
            dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
            if LiveVirtual_( v, base_ ) andalso (v->kind <> TK_SURF_TOOLTIP) then
                if (px >= v->vx) andalso (py >= v->vy) andalso (px < v->vx + v->vw) andalso (py < v->vy + v->vh) then t = v : exit for
                ' a modal surface keeps the pointer: what falls outside it is no one else's
                if (v->kind = TK_SURF_DIALOG) orelse (v->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN) then t = v : exit for
            end if
        next
    end if
    if t = 0 then t = base_
    dim as single ox = base_->ix / base_->fDensity, oy = base_->iy / base_->fDensity
    if t->bVirtual then ox += t->vx / base_->fDensity : oy += t->vy / base_->fDensity
    if (ox <> 0) orelse (oy <> 0) then
        select case e->type
        case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION : ev.motion.x -= ox : ev.motion.y -= oy
        case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP : ev.button.x -= ox : ev.button.y -= oy
        case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL : ev.wheel.mouse_x -= ox : ev.wheel.mouse_y -= oy
        case SDL_EVENT_DROP_COMPLETE : ev.drop.x -= ox : ev.drop.y -= oy
        end select
    end if
    ' the pointer moved to another surface: the one it left loses its hot widget, as a window
    ' the mouse leaves gets SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MOUSE_LEAVE
    if (gMouseHost <> 0) andalso (gMouseHost <> t) andalso (gMouseHost->bClosed = false) andalso (gMouseHost->pCapture = 0) then SetHot( gMouseHost, 0 )
    gMouseHost = t
    return t
end function

' On a base's resize: pages keep covering it, dialogs are centred again, popups close -- as a
' window's popups close when the window moves.
private sub RelayoutVirtual_( byval base_ as TK_HOST ptr )
    for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
        if i >= gnHosts then continue for
        dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
        if v->bVirtual andalso (v->pBase = base_) andalso (v->bClosed = false) then
            select case v->kind
            case TK_SURF_MAIN
                v->vw = base_->root->cw : v->vh = base_->root->ch
                SizeRoot( v )
                if v->OnSize then v->OnSize( v )
            case TK_SURF_DIALOG
                if v->vw > base_->root->cw then v->vw = base_->root->cw
                if v->vh > base_->root->ch then v->vh = base_->root->ch
                v->vx = (base_->root->cw - v->vw) \ 2 : v->vy = (base_->root->ch - v->vh) \ 2
                SizeRoot( v )
                if v->OnSize then v->OnSize( v )
            case else
                tkHost_Close( v )
            end select
            v->bDirty = true
        end if
    next
end sub

' ---- touch gestures (see top) ----------------------------------------------------------------
const TK_LONGPRESS_MS = 500
const TK_TOUCH_SLOP_DP = 8           ' how far a finger moves before it is a drag, in design units
const TK_TOUCH_NOTCH_DP = 60         ' finger travel per wheel notch: about three rows of a list
dim shared as Uint32 gEvTouch        ' this module's event: code 1 long-press, 2 fling step, 3 tap timeout
dim shared as long gTouchMode        ' 0 none, 1 pressed, 2 scrolling, 3 long-pressed
dim shared as SDL_FingerID gTouchFinger
dim shared as SDL_WindowID gTouchWin
dim shared as single gTouchX0, gTouchY0, gTouchX, gTouchY    ' window coordinates
dim shared as single gTouchVX, gTouchVY                      ' window units per ms, while scrolling
dim shared as Uint64 gTouchT
dim shared as long gTouchSerial
dim shared as single gFlingVX, gFlingVY
const TK_PRESS_DELAY_MS = 120
dim shared as boolean gPressHeld     ' SDL's touch-mouse press, held (see top)
dim shared as boolean gPressSent     ' ...and delivered
dim shared as SDL_WindowID gPressWin
dim shared as single gPressX, gPressY

private function TouchTick_( byval userdata as any ptr, byval timerID as SDL_TimerID, byval interval as Uint32 ) as Uint32
    dim as SDL_Event e
    e.type = gEvTouch
    e.user.code = cast( long, cast( integer, userdata ) and &hFFFF )
    e.user.data1 = cast( any ptr, cast( integer, userdata ) shr 16 )
    SDL_PushEvent( @e )
    return 0
end function

private sub PushMouse_( byval t as Uint32, byval wid as SDL_WindowID, byval x as single, byval y as single, byval btn as Uint8 )
    dim as SDL_Event e
    e.type = t
    e.button.windowID = wid
    e.button.which = 0                  ' not SDL_TOUCH_MOUSEID: these are the layer's own
    e.button.button = btn
    e.button.down = (t = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN)
    e.button.clicks = 1
    e.button.x = x : e.button.y = y
    SDL_PushEvent( @e )
end sub

private sub PushWheel_( byval wid as SDL_WindowID, byval x as single, byval y as single, byval wx as single, byval wy as single )
    dim as SDL_Event e
    e.type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_WHEEL
    e.wheel.windowID = wid
    e.wheel.which = 0
    e.wheel.x = wx : e.wheel.y = wy
    e.wheel.mouse_x = x : e.wheel.mouse_y = y
    e.wheel.direction = SDL_MOUSEWHEEL_NORMAL
    SDL_PushEvent( @e )
end sub

' The press the touched widget already has, taken back: released far outside it.
private sub CancelPress_()
    PushMouse_( SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP, gTouchWin, -100000, -100000, SDL_BUTTON_LEFT )
end sub

' Finger travel in window units as wheel notches, for the window's base surface.
private function NotchUnits_( byval wid as SDL_WindowID ) as single
    dim as TK_HOST ptr b = HostOfWindow( wid )
    dim as single sc = 1, d = 1
    if b then sc = b->fScale : d = b->fDensity
    return TK_TOUCH_NOTCH_DP * sc / d
end function

' TRUE = the event is the gesture layer's (consumed).
private sub SendHeldPress_()
    if gPressHeld andalso (gPressSent = false) then
        gPressSent = true
        PushMouse_( SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, gPressWin, gPressX, gPressY, SDL_BUTTON_LEFT )
    end if
end sub

' TRUE = the event is the gesture layer's (consumed).
private function Touch_( byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean
    if gEvTouch = 0 then gEvTouch = SDL_RegisterEvents( 1 )
    select case e->type
    case SDL_EVENT_FINGER_DOWN
        if gTouchMode <> 0 then return true          ' one finger drives; the rest are ignored
        dim as SDL_Window ptr w = SDL_GetWindowFromID( e->tfinger.windowID )
        if w = 0 then return true
        dim as long ww, wh
        SDL_GetWindowSize( w, @ww, @wh )
        gTouchFinger = e->tfinger.fingerID : gTouchWin = e->tfinger.windowID
        gTouchX0 = e->tfinger.x * ww : gTouchY0 = e->tfinger.y * wh
        gTouchX = gTouchX0 : gTouchY = gTouchY0
        gTouchVX = 0 : gTouchVY = 0 : gTouchT = SDL_GetTicks()
        gFlingVX = 0 : gFlingVY = 0
        gTouchMode = 1
        gTouchSerial += 1
        dim as integer ser = (gTouchSerial and &hFFFF) shl 16
        SDL_AddTimer( TK_PRESS_DELAY_MS, @TouchTick_, cast( any ptr, ser or 3 ) )
        SDL_AddTimer( TK_LONGPRESS_MS, @TouchTick_, cast( any ptr, ser or 1 ) )
        return true
    case SDL_EVENT_FINGER_MOTION
        if (gTouchMode = 0) orelse (e->tfinger.fingerID <> gTouchFinger) then return true
        dim as SDL_Window ptr w = SDL_GetWindowFromID( e->tfinger.windowID )
        if w = 0 then return true
        dim as long ww, wh
        SDL_GetWindowSize( w, @ww, @wh )
        dim as single x = e->tfinger.x * ww, y = e->tfinger.y * wh
        if gTouchMode = 1 then
            dim as TK_HOST ptr b = HostOfWindow( gTouchWin )
            dim as single slop = TK_TOUCH_SLOP_DP * iif( b <> 0, b->fScale / b->fDensity, 1.0 )
            if (abs( x - gTouchX0 ) > slop) orelse (abs( y - gTouchY0 ) > slop) then
                gTouchMode = 2
                if gPressSent then CancelPress_()
            end if
        end if
        if gTouchMode = 2 then
            dim as single n = NotchUnits_( gTouchWin )
            dim as single dx = x - gTouchX, dy = y - gTouchY
            if (dx <> 0) orelse (dy <> 0) then PushWheel_( gTouchWin, gTouchX0, gTouchY0, -dx / n, dy / n )
            dim as Uint64 now = SDL_GetTicks()
            dim as single dt = iif( now > gTouchT, now - gTouchT, 1 )
            gTouchVX = 0.6 * gTouchVX + 0.4 * (dx / dt) : gTouchVY = 0.6 * gTouchVY + 0.4 * (dy / dt)
            gTouchT = now
        end if
        gTouchX = x : gTouchY = y
        return true
    case SDL_EVENT_FINGER_UP, SDL_EVENT_FINGER_CANCELED
        if (gTouchMode = 0) orelse (e->tfinger.fingerID <> gTouchFinger) then return true
        ' a scroll that was still moving goes on, slowing: the fling
        if (gTouchMode = 2) andalso ((abs( gTouchVX ) + abs( gTouchVY )) > 0.3) andalso (SDL_GetTicks() - gTouchT < 100) then
            gFlingVX = gTouchVX : gFlingVY = gTouchVY
            gTouchSerial += 1
            SDL_AddTimer( 16, @TouchTick_, cast( any ptr, cast( integer, ((gTouchSerial and &hFFFF) shl 16) or 2 ) ) )
        end if
        gTouchMode = 0
        gPressHeld = false : gPressSent = false
        ' the finger is gone: so is the pointer (hover, tooltips)
        dim as SDL_Event lv
        lv.type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MOUSE_LEAVE
        lv.window.windowID = gTouchWin
        SDL_PushEvent( @lv )
        return true
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION
        if e->motion.which <> SDL_TOUCH_MOUSEID then return false
        ' held back until a press is delivered, and while the layer has the gesture
        return (gPressSent = false) orelse (gTouchMode = 2) orelse (gTouchMode = 3)
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP
        if e->button.which <> SDL_TOUCH_MOUSEID then return false
        if e->type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN then
            ' held (see top): it arrives before the finger does
            gPressHeld = true : gPressSent = false
            gPressWin = e->button.windowID : gPressX = e->button.x : gPressY = e->button.y
            return true
        end if
        ' the release: nothing of a scroll or a long-press; a tap delivers its press with it
        if (gTouchMode = 2) orelse (gTouchMode = 3) then return true
        if gPressSent then return false
        if gPressHeld then
            SendHeldPress_()
            PushMouse_( SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP, e->button.windowID, e->button.x, e->button.y, SDL_BUTTON_LEFT )
        end if
        return true
    end select
    if (gEvTouch <> 0) andalso (e->type = gEvTouch) then
        if cast( long, cast( integer, e->user.data1 ) ) <> (gTouchSerial and &hFFFF) then return true
        select case e->user.code
        case 3      ' the tap timeout: a finger still down and still gets its press
            if gTouchMode = 1 then SendHeldPress_()
        case 1      ' long-press: still pressed and still
            if gTouchMode = 1 then
                gTouchMode = 3
                if gPressSent then CancelPress_()
                PushMouse_( SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN, gTouchWin, gTouchX, gTouchY, SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT )
                PushMouse_( SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP, gTouchWin, gTouchX, gTouchY, SDL_BUTTON_RIGHT )
            end if
        case 2      ' a fling step
            gFlingVX *= 0.95 : gFlingVY *= 0.95
            dim as single n = NotchUnits_( gTouchWin )
            if (abs( gFlingVX ) + abs( gFlingVY )) * 16 > 0.5 then
                PushWheel_( gTouchWin, gTouchX0, gTouchY0, -gFlingVX * 16 / n, gFlingVY * 16 / n )
                SDL_AddTimer( 16, @TouchTick_, cast( any ptr, cast( integer, ((gTouchSerial and &hFFFF) shl 16) or 2 ) ) )
            end if
        end select
        return true
    end if
    return false
end function

' BACK: the top popup closes; else the top dialog or page gets the close its button would send;
' else the surface the key came to does (its window: the app's close, OnCloseRequest's to veto).
private sub Back_( byval target as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as TK_HOST ptr tp = TopPopup()
    if tp then tkHost_Close( tp ) : exit sub
    dim as TK_HOST ptr t = target
    for i as long = gnHosts - 1 to 0 step -1
        dim as TK_HOST ptr v = gHosts(i)
        if v->bVirtual andalso v->bShown andalso (v->bClosed = false) andalso ((v->kind = TK_SURF_DIALOG) orelse (v->kind = TK_SURF_MAIN)) then t = v : exit for
    next
    if t = 0 then exit sub
    dim as SDL_Event c
    c.type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_CLOSE_REQUESTED
    c.window.windowID = t->winId
    gDispatching += 1
    DispatchTo( t, @c )
    gDispatching -= 1
end sub

' One SDL event, routed to the surface it belongs to. The `h` argument is kept for callers of
' the single-window API and is used only for SDL_EVENT_QUIT.
public sub tkHost_Dispatch( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr )
    if e = 0 then exit sub
    if (gOnEvent <> 0) andalso gOnEvent( e ) then exit sub
    for i as long = 0 to ubound( gHooks )
        if (gHooks(i) <> 0) andalso gHooks(i)( e ) then exit sub
    next
    if gTrace < 0 then gTrace = iif( environ( "TK_TRACE" ) = "1", 1, 0 )
    if Virtual_() andalso Touch_( e ) then exit sub
    dim as SDL_WindowID wid = EventWindow( e )
    dim as TK_HOST ptr target = iif( wid <> 0, HostOfWindow( wid ), cast( TK_HOST ptr, 0 ) )
    ' VIRTUAL: the surface inside the window, and the event in its coordinates
    dim as SDL_Event ev
    if (target <> 0) andalso Virtual_() andalso (target->bVirtual = false) then
        target = VirtualTarget_( target, e, ev )
        e = @ev
    end if
    ' TK_TRACE=1: one line per event -- the trace that separates "SDL never sent it" from "it
    ' went elsewhere".
    if gTrace = 1 then
        print "ev " & hex( e->type ) & " win=" & wid & " host=" & iif( target <> 0, target->kind, -1 ) & _
              iif( e->type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION, " xy=" & e->motion.x & "," & e->motion.y, "" )
    end if

    select case e->type
    case SDL_EVENT_QUIT
        for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
            gHosts(i)->bQuit = true
        next
        if h then h->bQuit = true
        exit sub
    case SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_DOWN
        gPressSerial += 1
        ' the dismissal rule runs BEFORE the press is delivered
        if DismissFor( target ) then exit sub
    case SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN, SDL_EVENT_KEY_UP, SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT, SDL_EVENT_TEXT_EDITING
        ' BACK goes back a level (see top); its release is BACK's too
        if Virtual_() andalso ((e->type = SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN) orelse (e->type = SDL_EVENT_KEY_UP)) andalso (e->key.key = SDLK_AC_BACK) then
            ' with the soft keyboard up, BACK is the keyboard's: SDL hides it on the key's release (its
            ' SDLDummyEdit) and still sends the key, which closed an edit page too (measured, A5 step 8)
            if (e->type = SDL_EVENT_KEY_DOWN) andalso (e->key.repeat = false) then
                if SDL_ScreenKeyboardShown( target->win ) = false then Back_( target )
            end if
            exit sub
        end if
        ' keys go to the top popup while one is up, even when the compositor still routes them
        ' to the owner -- otherwise the arrows would drive whatever had focus behind it
        dim as TK_HOST ptr tp = TopPopup()
        if tp then target = tp
    end select

    if (gEvFocusCheck <> 0) andalso (e->type = gEvFocusCheck) then FocusCheck() : exit sub
    if (gEvTimer <> 0) andalso (e->type = gEvTimer) then
        dim as TK_TIMER ptr t = cast( TK_TIMER ptr, e->user.data1 )
        ' drop a tick that was already queued when its timer was killed
        if t andalso t->active andalso (t->gen = e->user.code) andalso (t->id = TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART) then
            dim as TK_WIDGET ptr tw = t->pW
            tkWidget_KillTimer( tw, TK_TIMER_TEXTRESTART )
            dim as TK_HOST ptr th = tw->pHost
            if (th <> 0) andalso th->bTextInput andalso (th->pFocus <> 0) andalso th->pFocus->bWantsText then StartText_( th, th->pFocus )
        elseif t andalso t->active andalso (t->gen = e->user.code) then
            dim as TK_MSG m
            m.msg = TKM_TIMER
            m.timerId = t->id
            gDispatching += 1
            tkWidget_Send( t->pW, @m )
            gDispatching -= 1
        end if
        exit sub
    end if

    if (target <> 0) andalso (target->bClosed = false) then
        gDispatching += 1
        DispatchTo( target, e )
        gDispatching -= 1
        if Virtual_() andalso (target->bClosed = false) then
            if ((e->type = SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_BUTTON_UP) andalso (e->button.button = SDL_BUTTON_LEFT)) orelse _
               (e->type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_FOCUS_GAINED) then KeyboardAgain_( target )
        end if
        if target->bVirtual = false andalso Virtual_() then
            if (e->type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED) orelse (e->type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED) then RelayoutVirtual_( target )
            ' the bars moved (rotation): the tree's safe area did
            if e->type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_SAFE_AREA_CHANGED then
                SizeRoot( target )
                if target->OnSize then target->OnSize( target )
                target->bDirty = true
                RelayoutVirtual_( target )
            end if
            ' the pointer left the window, so every surface in it: their hot widgets go too
            if e->type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_MOUSE_LEAVE then
                for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
                    if LiveVirtual_( gHosts(i), target ) andalso (gHosts(i)->pCapture = 0) then SetHot( gHosts(i), 0 )
                next
            end if
        end if
    end if
end sub

private sub RenderDirty()
    ' a dirty virtual surface is a dirty base: the window is painted once, whole
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if gHosts(i)->bVirtual andalso gHosts(i)->bDirty then
            gHosts(i)->bDirty = false
            if gHosts(i)->bClosed = false then gHosts(i)->pBase->bDirty = true
        end if
    next
    for i as long = 0 to gnHosts - 1
        if (gHosts(i)->bVirtual = false) andalso gHosts(i)->bDirty andalso (gHosts(i)->bClosed = false) then tkHost_Render( gHosts(i) )
    next
end sub

' Drain every queued event, reap closed surfaces, paint each dirty surface once. Non-blocking:
' the self-tests drive the host with this after pushing synthetic events.
'
' SDL3 ENDS A PollEvent ROUND AT A SENTINEL: events pushed after the round began -- including a
' test's own push, if an earlier round left a sentinel behind -- are not returned by that loop.
' A pump that stops at the first `false` can therefore return with the event its caller just
' pushed still queued (measured: the first synthetic motion of a second test pass never arrived).
' Each round can also bring the window events of a popup that just mapped -- on Wayland enough
' that four rounds left a pushed key queued (measured: 2 runs in 4). So drain until the queue is
' EMPTY, with a generous cap only so a timer that refills it every few ms cannot spin forever.
public sub tkHost_Pump( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    dim as SDL_Event e
    for round as long = 1 to 64
        while SDL_PollEvent( @e )
            tkHost_Dispatch( h, @e )
            tkHost_Reap()
        wend
        if SDL_HasEvents( SDL_EVENT_FIRST, SDL_EVENT_LAST ) = false then exit for
    next
    ' a virtual surface closes without a window event to pump, so nothing above reaped it
    if Virtual_() then tkHost_Reap()
    RenderDirty()
end sub

' The message loop. It BLOCKS in SDL_WaitEvent: an idle window costs nothing, unlike a game
' loop presenting 60 frames a second whether anything changed or not.
public sub tkHost_Run( byval h as TK_HOST ptr )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    RenderDirty()
    dim as SDL_Event e
    while h->bQuit = false
        if SDL_WaitEvent( @e ) then
            tkHost_Dispatch( h, @e )
            tkHost_Reap()
            while SDL_PollEvent( @e )
                tkHost_Dispatch( h, @e )
                tkHost_Reap()
            wend
        end if
        RenderDirty()
    wend
end sub


' ---- modal dialogs -----------------------------------------------------------------------
' Is event `e` for the dialog (or a popup it owns)? Everything else is DROPPED, never handed to
' the owner -- the owner is not supposed to be getting input while the dialog is modal.
private function ForDialog( byval dlg as TK_HOST ptr, byval e as SDL_Event ptr ) as boolean
    dim as SDL_WindowID wid = EventWindow( e )
    if wid = 0 then return true                 ' timers, quit: not window events
    dim as TK_HOST ptr t = HostOfWindow( wid )
    if t = 0 then return false
    ' virtual: the surface the router would pick (a window event stays the base's, and so is the
    ' owner's to repaint, not the dialog's input)
    if Virtual_() andalso (t->bVirtual = false) then
        dim as SDL_Event ev
        dim as TK_HOST ptr saved = gMouseHost
        t = VirtualTarget_( t, e, ev )
        gMouseHost = saved
    end if
    return InChainOf( t, dlg )
end function

' Show `dlg` modally and pump until tkHost_EndModal (or its close button with no
' OnCloseRequest). Returns the result. A QUIT ends the dialog AND is re-posted, so the outer loop
' still sees it. The owner keeps being repainted (expose) but gets no input.
public function tkHost_RunModal( byval dlg as TK_HOST ptr ) as long
    if dlg = 0 then return 0
    if (dlg->pOwner <> 0) andalso (dlg->bVirtual = false) then SDL_SetWindowModal( dlg->win, true )
    tkHost_Show( dlg )
    if dlg->pFocus = 0 then tkHost_FocusNext( dlg )
    dlg->bEndModal = false
    dim as SDL_Event e
    RenderDirty()
    while dlg->bEndModal = false
        if SDL_WaitEvent( @e ) = false then continue while
        do
            if e.type = SDL_EVENT_QUIT then
                dlg->bEndModal = true
                SDL_PushEvent( @e )
                exit do
            end if
            dim as SDL_WindowID wid = EventWindow( @e )
            if ForDialog( dlg, @e ) then
                tkHost_Dispatch( dlg, @e )
            elseif (e.type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_EXPOSED) orelse (e.type = SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED) then
                dim as TK_HOST ptr t = HostOfWindow( wid )
                if t then DispatchTo( t, @e )
            end if
            tkHost_Reap()
            if dlg->bEndModal then exit do
        loop while SDL_PollEvent( @e )
        RenderDirty()
    wend
    dim as long r = dlg->nModalResult
    ' Hand activation back to the owner WHILE the dialog is still shown, as EndDialog does:
    ' re-enable it, then activate it. Hiding the active dialog first lets the OS activate the
    ' next window in z-order -- often another application's -- and the owner, still disabled
    ' or merely behind, never gets it back.
    if (dlg->pOwner <> 0) andalso dlg->bVirtual then
        dlg->pOwner->bDirty = true
    elseif dlg->pOwner then
        SDL_SetWindowModal( dlg->win, false )
        if (SDL_GetWindowFlags( dlg->pOwner->win ) and SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN) = 0 then SDL_RaiseWindow( dlg->pOwner->win )
        dlg->pOwner->bDirty = true
    end if
    return r
end function

public sub tkHost_EndModal( byval dlg as TK_HOST ptr, byval result as long )
    if dlg = 0 then exit sub
    dlg->nModalResult = result
    dlg->bEndModal = true
end sub

' The caption band of a borderless dialog: a press there drags the window.
private function HitTestCb( byval win as SDL_Window ptr, byval area as const SDL_Point ptr, _
                            byval data_ as any ptr ) as SDL_HitTestResult
    dim as TK_HOST ptr h = cast( TK_HOST ptr, data_ )
    if (h = 0) orelse (area = 0) then return SDL_HITTEST_NORMAL
    dim as single px = area->x * h->fDensity, py = area->y * h->fDensity
    if tkRect_Contains( h->rcDrag, px, py ) then
        ' a widget on the band (a close button) keeps its clicks
        dim as TK_WIDGET ptr w = tkHost_HitTest( h, px, py )
        if (w = 0) orelse (w->isFocusable = false) then return SDL_HITTEST_DRAGGABLE
    end if
    return SDL_HITTEST_NORMAL
end function

public sub tkHost_SetDragRect( byval h as TK_HOST ptr, byref rc as TKRECT )
    if h = 0 then exit sub
    h->rcDrag = rc
    if h->bVirtual = false then SDL_SetWindowHitTest( h->win, @HitTestCb, h )
end sub


' ---- clipboard -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
public sub tkHost_SetClipboardText( byref s as ustring )
    dim as string u8 = s
    SDL_SetClipboardText( strptr( u8 ) )
end sub

public function tkHost_GetClipboardText() as ustring
    dim as zstring ptr p = SDL_GetClipboardText()
    if p = 0 then return ""
    dim as string u8 = *p
    SDL_free( p )
    dim as ustring s = u8
    return s
end function

public function tkHost_HasClipboardText() as boolean
    return SDL_HasClipboardText()
end function
